msgstr "Video ini memberikan gambaran keseluruhan teknik pengurangan ralat. Teks di bawah menambah lebih banyak butiran dan meneroka kaedah-kaedah ini menggunakan Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"135049030\" title=\"In this video, Chris Porter provides an overview of quantum error mitigation. Matrix-free measurement mitigation, twirled readout error extinction, zero-noise extrapolation, and probabilistic error cancellation are discussed.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"135049030\" title=\"Dalam video ini, Chris Porter memberikan gambaran keseluruhan pengurangan ralat kuantum. Pengurangan pengukuran tanpa matriks, pemupusan ralat bacaan terpilin, ekstrapolasi hingar sifar, dan pembatalan ralat probabilistik dibincangkan.\"/>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of error mitigation techniques {#overview-of-error-mitigation-techniques}"
msgstr "Gambaran keseluruhan teknik pengurangan ralat {#overview-of-error-mitigation-techniques}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error mitigation refers to any process that attempts to reduce the effects of errors in quantum computations after they have occurred. It is different from suppression, which attempts to prevent errors, and from error correction, which encodes information across many physical qubits and checks the consistency in that information to preserve information in a single logical qubit. Throughout this lesson, error mitigation techniques can best be understood as methods for constructing better estimators of ideal expectation values or better samplers of probability distributions, **not** as methods for correcting quantum states during execution. We will examine the error mitigation methods below, all of which are available in Qiskit and its addons, and which are promising tools in the pursuit of quantum advantage.\n"
msgstr "Pengurangan ralat merujuk kepada sebarang proses yang cuba mengurangkan kesan ralat dalam pengiraan kuantum selepas ralat itu berlaku. Ia berbeza daripada penindasan, yang cuba mencegah ralat, dan daripada pembetulan ralat, yang mengekod maklumat merentasi banyak qubit fizikal dan menyemak ketekalan maklumat tersebut untuk memelihara maklumat dalam satu qubit logik. Sepanjang pelajaran ini, teknik pengurangan ralat paling baik difahami sebagai kaedah untuk membina penganggar jangkaan nilai unggul yang lebih baik atau pensampel taburan kebarangkalian yang lebih baik, **bukan** sebagai kaedah untuk membetulkan keadaan kuantum semasa pelaksanaan. Kita akan meneliti kaedah pengurangan ralat di bawah, yang kesemuanya tersedia dalam Qiskit dan addon-nya, dan merupakan alat yang menjanjikan dalam usaha mencapai kelebihan kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Twirled readout error extinction (TREX)** randomizes the measurement process by applying randomly selected Pauli operations before measurement and then classically undoing their known effects on the observed bitstrings. Under suitable measurement-noise assumptions, this converts the readout error channel into a simpler and more symmetric form that is easier to calibrate and mitigate.\n"
msgstr "**Twirled readout error extinction (TREX)** merawakkan proses pengukuran dengan menggunakan operasi Pauli yang dipilih secara rawak sebelum pengukuran dan kemudian membatalkan kesan yang diketahui itu secara klasik pada rentetan bit yang diperhatikan. Di bawah andaian hingar pengukuran yang sesuai, ini menukar saluran ralat bacaan kepada bentuk yang lebih ringkas dan lebih simetri yang lebih mudah ditentukur dan dikurangkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Matrix-free measurement mitigation (M3)** is a scalable measurement-error mitigation technique that avoids explicitly constructing the assignment matrix or its inverse.\n"
msgstr "**Matrix-free measurement mitigation (M3)** ialah teknik pengurangan ralat pengukuran berskala yang mengelakkan pembinaan matriks penugasan atau songsangannya secara eksplisit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Zero noise extrapolation (ZNE)** approximates the value an observable would have in the absence of noise by artificially scaling noise by a known factor and extrapolating back to the zero-noise case. This requires that noise scale in a predictable way. That predictability might require other methods discussed in this lesson (pulse stretching, gate folding, and probabilistic error amplification (PEA)).\n"
msgstr "**Zero noise extrapolation (ZNE)** menganggarkan nilai yang akan dimiliki oleh suatu observable tanpa hingar dengan menskalakan hingar secara buatan mengikut faktor yang diketahui dan mengekstrapolasi kembali kepada kes hingar sifar. Ini memerlukan hingar berskala dengan cara yang boleh diramal. Kebolehramalan itu mungkin memerlukan kaedah lain yang dibincangkan dalam pelajaran ini (regangan denyut, pelipatan gate, dan penguatan ralat probabilistik (PEA)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)** is among the most powerful, but also the most computationally expensive, error-mitigation techniques. It works by learning the noise behavior of the system and attempting to undo the noise by statistically constructing an unbiased estimate of the ideal computation. PEC outputs statistically corrected observables, not error-corrected results.\n"
msgstr "**Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC)** ialah antara teknik pengurangan ralat yang paling berkuasa, tetapi juga paling mahal dari segi pengiraan. Ia berfungsi dengan mempelajari tingkah laku hingar sistem dan cuba membatalkan hingar itu dengan membina anggaran tidak berat sebelah bagi pengiraan unggul secara statistik. PEC menghasilkan observable yang dibetulkan secara statistik, bukan keputusan yang dibetulkan ralatnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will now dive into each of these methods.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini akan mendalami setiap kaedah ini.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "M3 {#m3}"
msgstr "M3 {#m3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurement errors are one of the most persistent and hardware-specific sources of noise in near-term quantum devices. Even when a quantum state is prepared and evolved correctly, the final readout step can misreport the true computational basis outcome. These errors arise from imperfect discrimination between the physical states corresponding to $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, relaxation during measurement, and imperfections in measurement electronics. As a result, the observed distribution of bitstrings is often a distorted version of the true (ideal) distribution, with probability incorrectly reassigned between outcomes.\n"
msgstr "Ralat pengukuran ialah salah satu sumber hingar yang paling berterusan dan khusus perkakasan dalam peranti kuantum jangka dekat. Walaupun keadaan kuantum disediakan dan berkembang dengan betul, langkah bacaan akhir boleh tersalah melaporkan hasil asas pengiraan yang sebenar. Ralat ini timbul daripada pembezaan tidak sempurna antara keadaan fizikal yang sepadan dengan $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$, relaksasi semasa pengukuran, dan ketidaksempurnaan dalam elektronik pengukuran. Akibatnya, taburan rentetan bit yang diperhatikan selalunya versi herot bagi taburan sebenar (unggul), dengan kebarangkalian ditugaskan semula secara tidak betul antara hasil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurement mitigation addresses this problem by explicitly modeling how measurement outcomes are misassigned. In the standard formulation, this behavior is captured by an assignment matrix $A$, whose elements $A_{ij}$ represent the probability of recording outcome $i$ when the true basis state was $j$. If the measurement noise is classical and stationary, the observed probability vector $p_{\\text{obs}}$ is related to the ideal distribution $p_{\\text{ideal}}$ by a simple linear relation,\n"
"$$\n"
"p_{\\text{obs}} = A\\, p_{\\text{ideal}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengurangan pengukuran menangani masalah ini dengan memodelkan secara eksplisit bagaimana hasil pengukuran tersalah ditugaskan. Dalam formulasi piawai, tingkah laku ini ditangkap oleh matriks penugasan $A$, yang unsurnya $A_{ij}$ mewakili kebarangkalian merekodkan hasil $i$ apabila keadaan asas sebenar ialah $j$. Jika hingar pengukuran bersifat klasik dan pegun, vektor kebarangkalian yang diperhatikan $p_{\\text{obs}}$ berkaitan dengan taburan unggul $p_{\\text{ideal}}$ melalui hubungan linear yang ringkas,\n"
"$$\n"
"p_{\\text{obs}} = A\\, p_{\\text{ideal}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the assignment matrix $A$ is a classical stochastic map, not a quantum channel. It acts on classical readouts, not on the underlying quantum states that were sampled to obtain the readouts.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa matriks penugasan $A$ ialah peta stokastik klasik, bukan saluran kuantum. Ia bertindak pada bacaan klasik, bukan pada keadaan kuantum asas yang disampel untuk mendapatkan bacaan tersebut.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A histogram of many measurements. Two matrices are also shown. One is a full assignment matrix describing all possible measurements. The other is a reduced matrix functioning as an assignment matrix only in the subspace of measured states.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/m3-counts.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A histogram of many measurements. Two matrices are also shown. One is a full assignment matrix describing all possible measurements. The other is a reduced matrix functioning as an assignment matrix only in the subspace of measured states.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/m3-counts.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix-free measurement mitigation (M3) uses this structure to construct a mitigated estimate of $p_{\\text{ideal}}$ without ever forming or inverting the full matrix $A$, which would be infeasible for large numbers of qubits. Instead, M3 exploits the fact that many near-term quantum workloads produce highly peaked or low-entropy distributions, so that mitigation focuses only on the subset of outcomes that significantly contribute to the observed distribution.\n"
msgstr "Matrix-free measurement mitigation (M3) menggunakan struktur ini untuk membina anggaran terkurang bagi $p_{\\text{ideal}}$ tanpa pernah membentuk atau menyongsangkan matriks penuh $A$, yang mustahil dilakukan untuk bilangan qubit yang besar. Sebaliknya, M3 memanfaatkan hakikat bahawa banyak beban kerja kuantum jangka dekat menghasilkan taburan yang sangat memuncak atau berentropi rendah, sehingga pengurangan hanya tertumpu pada subset hasil yang menyumbang dengan ketara kepada taburan yang diperhatikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To build the assignment model, additional calibration experiments must be run on the quantum hardware. These typically involve preparing known computational basis states and recording how they are reported by the measurement system. The calibration overhead scales with the number of measured qubits, while the computational cost of mitigation depends on the structure of the observed distribution. This cost is far smaller than what would be required to characterize the full $2^n \\times 2^n$ assignment matrix explicitly. While this calibration overhead is real, it is lightweight compared to circuit-level techniques like zero-noise extrapolation or probabilistic error cancellation, making M3 a practical and widely used tool for mitigating readout errors in near-term quantum experiments.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membina model penugasan, eksperimen penentukuran tambahan mesti dijalankan pada perkakasan kuantum. Ini lazimnya melibatkan penyediaan keadaan asas pengiraan yang diketahui dan merekodkan cara keadaan itu dilaporkan oleh sistem pengukuran. Overhed penentukuran berskala dengan bilangan qubit yang diukur, manakala kos pengiraan pengurangan bergantung pada struktur taburan yang diperhatikan. Kos ini jauh lebih kecil daripada yang diperlukan untuk mencirikan matriks penugasan penuh $2^n \\times 2^n$ secara eksplisit. Walaupun overhed penentukuran ini wujud, ia ringan berbanding teknik peringkat litar seperti zero-noise extrapolation atau probabilistic error cancellation, menjadikan M3 alat yang praktikal dan digunakan secara meluas untuk mengurangkan ralat bacaan dalam eksperimen kuantum jangka dekat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that calibration is only useful to the extent that the measurement process remains sufficiently stable between the calibration runs and the target experiment.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa penentukuran hanya berguna setakat proses pengukuran kekal cukup stabil antara larian penentukuran dan eksperimen sasaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will first carry out a simple case by hand to illustrate how it works, then use tools built into Qiskit to show the use of M3 at a more realistic scale.\n"
msgstr "Kita mula-mula akan melaksanakan kes ringkas secara manual untuk menggambarkan cara ia berfungsi, kemudian menggunakan alat terbina dalam Qiskit untuk menunjukkan penggunaan M3 pada skala yang lebih realistik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "M3 small example {#m3-small-example}"
msgstr "Contoh kecil M3 {#m3-small-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start by building a simple Bell state.\n"
msgstr "Kita bermula dengan membina keadaan Bell yang ringkas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use a simulator with a noise model because we are restricting this example to a very small circuit. We explicitly configure our noise model to have readout error of the form:\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menggunakan simulator dengan model hingar kerana kita mengehadkan contoh ini kepada litar yang sangat kecil. Kita mengkonfigurasi model hingar kita secara eksplisit supaya mempunyai ralat bacaan dalam bentuk:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`if true=0: [95% chance of reading 0, 5% chance of reading 1]`\n"
msgstr "`if true=0: [95% chance of reading 0, 5% chance of reading 1]`\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`if true=1: [8% chance of reading 0, 92% chance of reading 1]`\n"
msgstr "`if true=1: [8% chance of reading 0, 92% chance of reading 1]`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These readout error rates are much higher than what one sees in real IBM&reg; quantum computers. The high values have been chosen for pedagogical reasons, so that we can clearly see the effect of M3.\n"
msgstr "Kadar ralat bacaan ini jauh lebih tinggi daripada yang dilihat pada komputer kuantum IBM&reg; sebenar. Nilai tinggi ini dipilih atas sebab pedagogi, supaya kita dapat melihat dengan jelas kesan M3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can run the circuit on the noisy simulator to observe the effects of readout error.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menjalankan litar pada simulator berhingar untuk memerhatikan kesan ralat bacaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In our toy example, **we defined the readout error** for our noise model. But when using a **real quantum computer**, the readout error is not known a priori. Instead, it must be estimated experimentally. For this, we create circuits to prepare a qubit in a known computational basis state $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ and measure it. In the absence of readout error we would measure exactly the prepared state. By collecting statistics from these measurements, we can build an assignment matrix describing the readout error. In this toy example, it should look similar to the one we defined.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh mainan kita, **kita mentakrifkan ralat bacaan** untuk model hingar kita. Tetapi apabila menggunakan **komputer kuantum sebenar**, ralat bacaan tidak diketahui secara a priori. Sebaliknya, ia mesti dianggarkan secara eksperimen. Untuk ini, kita mencipta litar untuk menyediakan qubit dalam keadaan asas pengiraan yang diketahui $|0\\rangle$ atau $|1\\rangle$ dan mengukurnya. Tanpa ralat bacaan, kita akan mengukur tepat keadaan yang disediakan. Dengan mengumpul statistik daripada pengukuran ini, kita boleh membina matriks penugasan yang menerangkan ralat bacaan. Dalam contoh mainan ini, ia sepatutnya kelihatan serupa dengan yang kita takrifkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a more realistic system, statistics would need to be accumulated for each physical qubit. This is sometimes non-trivial, because transpilation maps an abstract circuit to hardware and the qubit number changes. We will revisit that in the next example. In this simulator example, we assigned the same readout-error model to every qubit, so a single characterization is sufficient.\n"
msgstr "Untuk sistem yang lebih realistik, statistik perlu dikumpulkan bagi setiap qubit fizikal. Ini kadangkala tidak mudah, kerana transpilasi memetakan litar abstrak kepada perkakasan dan nombor qubit berubah. Kita akan menyemak semula perkara ini dalam contoh seterusnya. Dalam contoh simulator ini, kita menugaskan model ralat bacaan yang sama kepada setiap qubit, jadi satu pencirian sudah memadai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this is very close to the readout error matrix used to construct the simulator.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa ini sangat hampir dengan matriks ralat bacaan yang digunakan untuk membina simulator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Again, on a real quantum computer we would have statistics like these for multiple physical qubits. For this simulator, we assume the two qubits have identical and independent readout errors, allowing us to construct the two-qubit assignment matrix `A_2q` as a tensor product of the corresponding one-qubit matrices. Also note that the point of M3 is **not** to construct the entire assignment matrix. Instead, M3 focuses on the subset of outcomes that significantly contribute to the observed distribution. We will build the entire matrix for our very small example to see how it works. The implementation of M3 in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` is more sophisticated than this toy example because it must handle many qubits with distinct readout characteristics while still avoiding construction of the full assignment matrix.\n"
msgstr "Sekali lagi, pada komputer kuantum sebenar kita akan mempunyai statistik seperti ini untuk berbilang qubit fizikal. Bagi simulator ini, kita menganggap kedua-dua qubit mempunyai ralat bacaan yang serupa dan bebas, membolehkan kita membina matriks penugasan dua-qubit `A_2q` sebagai hasil darab tensor matriks satu-qubit yang sepadan. Perhatikan juga bahawa tujuan M3 ialah **bukan** untuk membina keseluruhan matriks penugasan. Sebaliknya, M3 menumpukan pada subset hasil yang menyumbang dengan ketara kepada taburan yang diperhatikan. Kita akan membina keseluruhan matriks untuk contoh kita yang sangat kecil ini bagi melihat cara ia berfungsi. Pelaksanaan M3 dalam `qiskit-ibm-runtime` lebih canggih daripada contoh mainan ini kerana ia mesti mengendalikan banyak qubit dengan ciri bacaan yang berbeza sambil tetap mengelakkan pembinaan matriks penugasan penuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this example we assume that readout errors on different qubits are independent, allowing the two-qubit assignment matrix to be constructed as a tensor product of the corresponding one-qubit matrices.\n"
msgstr "Untuk contoh ini kita menganggap ralat bacaan pada qubit berbeza adalah bebas, membolehkan matriks penugasan dua-qubit dibina sebagai hasil darab tensor matriks satu-qubit yang sepadan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We obtain the raw and mitigated results for comparison.\n"
msgstr "Kita memperoleh keputusan mentah dan terkurang untuk perbandingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point, we have experimentally characterized how the measurement process distorts ideal outcome probabilities. Our goal is now to undo this distortion and apply the resulting correction to the raw probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Pada ketika ini, kita telah mencirikan secara eksperimen cara proses pengukuran memesongkan kebarangkalian hasil unggul. Matlamat kita sekarang ialah membatalkan herotan ini dan menggunakan pembetulan yang terhasil pada kebarangkalian mentah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we are performing a linear inversion rather than a physical correction, the resulting \"probabilities\" need not always be positive. Very small negative quasi-probabilities are expected and reflect the fact that measurement mitigation produces an estimator rather than a physical probability distribution.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana kita melakukan penyongsangan linear dan bukannya pembetulan fizikal, \"kebarangkalian\" yang terhasil tidak semestinya sentiasa positif. Kuasi-kebarangkalian negatif yang sangat kecil dijangka dan mencerminkan hakikat bahawa pengurangan pengukuran menghasilkan penganggar dan bukannya taburan kebarangkalian fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We convert these to counts for plotting.\n"
msgstr "Kita menukarkannya kepada kiraan untuk diplot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally we look at the raw, mitigated, and ideal distributions. The mitigated \"counts\" below are only a visualization aid obtained by rescaling the mitigated quasi-probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali kita melihat taburan mentah, terkurang, dan unggul. \"Kiraan\" terkurang di bawah hanyalah alat bantu visualisasi yang diperoleh dengan menskala semula kuasi-kebarangkalian terkurang.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/f10a0dda-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/f10a0dda-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearly, the M3-mitigated results are much closer to the ideal distributions, and we can see why.\n"
msgstr "Jelas sekali, keputusan terkurang M3 jauh lebih dekat dengan taburan unggul, dan kita dapat melihat sebabnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying M3 to more realistic workflows is much more complex. Consider:\n"
"* Real quantum computers contain many physical qubits, each with its own readout-error characteristics. These errors must be modeled and combined appropriately.\n"
"* The full assignment matrix $A$ grows exponentially with the number of qubits and quickly becomes impractical to construct explicitly. This is why M3 focuses on the subset of outcomes that contribute significantly to the observed distribution rather than constructing the entire assignment matrix.\n"
"* For real problems of interest, the ideal distribution might not be known.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan M3 pada aliran kerja yang lebih realistik adalah jauh lebih kompleks. Pertimbangkan:\n"
"* Komputer kuantum sebenar mengandungi banyak qubit fizikal, masing-masing dengan ciri ralat bacaannya sendiri. Ralat ini mesti dimodelkan dan digabungkan dengan sewajarnya.\n"
"* Matriks penugasan penuh $A$ membesar secara eksponen dengan bilangan qubit dan dengan cepat menjadi tidak praktikal untuk dibina secara eksplisit. Inilah sebabnya M3 menumpukan pada subset hasil yang menyumbang dengan ketara kepada taburan yang diperhatikan dan bukannya membina keseluruhan matriks penugasan.\n"
"* Bagi masalah sebenar yang menarik, taburan unggul mungkin tidak diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For all of these reasons, the full mitigation workflow is encapsulated in the `mthree` Qiskit addon.\n"
msgstr "Atas semua sebab ini, aliran kerja pengurangan penuh dikapsulkan dalam addon Qiskit `mthree`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Larger M3 example {#larger-m3-example}"
msgstr "Contoh M3 yang lebih besar {#larger-m3-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now apply M3 to a larger circuit, one for which determining the relevant subspace of $A$ by hand would be cumbersome, but which is still simple enough that we know the ideal distribution: a GHZ state. We start importing the `mthree` package and defining a GHZ quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini menggunakan M3 pada litar yang lebih besar, yang mana penentuan subruang $A$ yang relevan secara manual akan menyusahkan, tetapi masih cukup ringkas supaya kita mengetahui taburan unggulnya: keadaan GHZ. Kita mulakan dengan mengimport pakej `mthree` dan mentakrifkan litar kuantum GHZ.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d7e4b190-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d7e4b190-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run this on a real quantum computer, we import `qiskit_ibm_runtime` and other necessary packages. We use `SamplerV2` to obtain a distribution of outputs.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan ini pada komputer kuantum sebenar, kita mengimport `qiskit_ibm_runtime` dan pakej lain yang diperlukan. Kita menggunakan `SamplerV2` untuk mendapatkan taburan output.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we transpile the circuit to our backend. We are setting the optimization level to 0 here in order to focus on the effects of M3, without adding in additional tools. This means the final fidelity will not be representative of what is achievable on IBM Quantum&reg; hardware using the full suite of available tools, but it allows us to focus specifically on the usefulness of M3.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita mentranspilasi litar ke Backend kita. Kita menetapkan tahap pengoptimuman kepada 0 di sini untuk menumpukan pada kesan M3, tanpa menambah alat tambahan. Ini bermakna fidelity akhir tidak mewakili apa yang boleh dicapai pada perkakasan IBM Quantum&reg; menggunakan set penuh alat yang tersedia, tetapi ia membolehkan kita menumpukan secara khusus pada kegunaan M3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now configure the Sampler, again disabling additional error-suppression techniques such as dynamical decoupling and twirling.\n"
msgstr "Kita kini mengkonfigurasi Sampler, sekali lagi melumpuhkan teknik penindasan ralat tambahan seperti dynamical decoupling dan twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we execute our job.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kita melaksanakan job kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can extract the raw counts from the circuit above.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh mengekstrak kiraan mentah daripada litar di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we run `mthree` on our backend to characterize the assignment model used for measurement mitigation. We rescale the raw distribution using that information. Note that this can sometimes result in very small negative probabilities (hence the term **quasi-probabilities**).\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita menjalankan `mthree` pada Backend kita untuk mencirikan model penugasan yang digunakan untuk pengurangan pengukuran. Kita menskala semula taburan mentah menggunakan maklumat tersebut. Perhatikan bahawa ini kadangkala boleh menghasilkan kebarangkalian negatif yang sangat kecil (maka istilah **kuasi-kebarangkalian**).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `mthree` correction produces quasi-probabilities, rather than counts. We can rescale to counts by hand. The helper function below converts to counts and rounds to integer values. Also, for large circuits, there will be many erroneous strings with very few counts, but which clutter a histogram. The second helper function below trims away any strings with fewer counts than some threshold we choose, to give us a clear view of the dominant terms in the distribution.\n"
msgstr "Pembetulan `mthree` menghasilkan kuasi-kebarangkalian, bukan kiraan. Kita boleh menskala semula kepada kiraan secara manual. Fungsi pembantu di bawah menukar kepada kiraan dan membundarkan kepada nilai integer. Selain itu, bagi litar besar, akan terdapat banyak rentetan yang salah dengan kiraan yang sangat sedikit, tetapi yang menyemakkan histogram. Fungsi pembantu kedua di bawah membuang sebarang rentetan dengan kiraan kurang daripada ambang yang kita pilih, supaya kita mendapat pandangan jelas tentang sebutan dominan dalam taburan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also easily produce the theoretical, ideal distribution in which we have equal probabilities for the all-zero and all-one states, and zero probability for all other outcomes, for comparison.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga boleh dengan mudah menghasilkan taburan unggul teori yang mempunyai kebarangkalian sama untuk keadaan semua-sifar dan semua-satu, dan kebarangkalian sifar untuk semua hasil lain, sebagai perbandingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we can visualize our results.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kita boleh memvisualisasikan keputusan kita.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/4a451fe6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/4a451fe6-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mitigated results are closer to the ideal distribution than the unmitigated results. We can quantify this better using counts for the ideal bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan terkurang lebih dekat dengan taburan unggul berbanding keputusan tidak terkurang. Kita boleh mengkuantifikasikan ini dengan lebih baik menggunakan kiraan bagi rentetan bit unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This simple tool improved our fidelity by 26% relative to the unmitigated fidelity, with fairly low overhead. Clearly M3 can be very valuable. But the GHZ circuit was selected as a good use case, because it is highly peaked on two output states. Some problems result in more evenly-distributed counts (high entropy states). For very deep circuits with many qubits, gate errors and noise unrelated to measurement errors will often result in a high-entropy state. In such cases, M3 operates on a state space that is quite large. There are three possible approaches to this:\n"
msgstr "Alat ringkas ini meningkatkan fidelity kita sebanyak 26% berbanding fidelity tidak terkurang, dengan overhed yang agak rendah. Jelas bahawa M3 boleh sangat bernilai. Tetapi litar GHZ dipilih sebagai kes penggunaan yang baik, kerana ia sangat memuncak pada dua keadaan output. Sesetengah masalah menghasilkan kiraan yang lebih sekata taburannya (keadaan entropi tinggi). Bagi litar yang sangat dalam dengan banyak qubit, ralat gate dan hingar yang tidak berkaitan dengan ralat pengukuran selalunya akan menghasilkan keadaan entropi tinggi. Dalam kes sedemikian, M3 beroperasi pada ruang keadaan yang agak besar. Terdapat tiga pendekatan yang mungkin untuk ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '(1) '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accept that this is a limitation of M3.\n"
msgstr "Terima bahawa ini adalah had M3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '(2) '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the upper bound on the space of the matrix formed by M3 is `num_shots` $\\times$ `num_shots`, rather than $2^N \\times 2^N$, with the former being much smaller for large number of qubits $N$.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa had atas ruang matriks yang dibentuk oleh M3 ialah `num_shots` $\\times$ `num_shots`, dan bukannya $2^N \\times 2^N$, dengan yang pertama jauh lebih kecil untuk bilangan qubit $N$ yang besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '(3) '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only with great caution, remove very low-probability bitstrings from the raw counts fed into M3. This might introduce bias, and the limitation of the support of your states can interfere with convergence in approaches like the Krylov method. This should only be done when you know exactly why you are doing it and can anticipate all its effects. That is why such trimming is not a built-in feature of M3.\n"
msgstr "Hanya dengan sangat berhati-hati, buang rentetan bit berkebarangkalian sangat rendah daripada kiraan mentah yang dimasukkan ke dalam M3. Ini mungkin memperkenalkan pincang, dan pengehadan sokongan keadaan anda boleh mengganggu penumpuan dalam pendekatan seperti kaedah Krylov. Ini hanya perlu dilakukan apabila anda tahu dengan tepat mengapa anda melakukannya dan dapat menjangka semua kesannya. Itulah sebabnya pemangkasan sedemikian bukan ciri terbina dalam M3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more on the `mthree` Qiskit addon see examples, installation instructions, background, and API references in its [documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mthree/).\n"
msgstr "Untuk maklumat lanjut tentang addon Qiskit `mthree`, lihat contoh, arahan pemasangan, latar belakang, dan rujukan API dalam [dokumentasi](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-mthree/) nya.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled readout error extinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"
msgstr "Twirled readout error extinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled Readout Error Extinction (TREX) is a measurement-error mitigation technique used on modern quantum computers. Its goal is to remove bias introduced by classical readout errors without requiring full characterization or inversion of the measurement assignment matrix.\n"
msgstr "Twirled Readout Error Extinction (TREX) ialah teknik pengurangan ralat pengukuran yang digunakan pada komputer kuantum moden. Matlamatnya ialah menghapuskan pincang yang diperkenalkan oleh ralat bacaan klasik tanpa memerlukan pencirian penuh atau penyongsangan matriks penugasan pengukuran.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX is not error correction and does not improve state fidelity. Instead, it ensures that expectation value estimators are unbiased with respect to readout noise, up to statistical error, by averaging over randomized measurement bases and rescaling. On IBM Quantum hardware, TREX is the default mitigation method for expectation-value estimation and corresponds to `resilience_level = 1` in the IBM Quantum Estimator primitive.\n"
msgstr "TREX bukan pembetulan ralat dan tidak meningkatkan fidelity keadaan. Sebaliknya, ia memastikan penganggar nilai jangkaan tidak berat sebelah terhadap hingar bacaan, sehingga ralat statistik, dengan mengambil purata ke atas asas pengukuran yang dirawakkan dan menskala semula. Pada perkakasan IBM Quantum, TREX ialah kaedah pengurangan lalai untuk anggaran nilai jangkaan dan sepadan dengan `resilience_level = 1` dalam primitif IBM Quantum Estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nature of readout errors on superconducting hardware {#nature-of-readout-errors-on-superconducting-hardware}"
msgstr "Sifat ralat bacaan pada perkakasan superkonduktor {#nature-of-readout-errors-on-superconducting-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On IBM superconducting qubits, readout errors are dominated by:\n"
msgstr "Pada qubit superkonduktor IBM, ralat bacaan didominasi oleh:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Asymmetric bit-flip probabilities (for example, $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ more frequently than the reverse)\n"
msgstr "Kebarangkalian pembalikan bit tak simetri (contohnya, $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ lebih kerap daripada sebaliknya)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "State-dependent relaxation during measurement itself\n"
msgstr "Relaksasi bergantung keadaan semasa pengukuran itu sendiri\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mild but non-negligible crosstalk between neighboring readout resonators\n"
msgstr "Gandingan silang yang ringan tetapi tidak boleh diabaikan antara resonator bacaan berjiran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Importantly, these errors can often be modeled as a classical stochastic process acting on measurement outcomes. TREX exploits a standard idea from noise tailoring: randomization (twirling) of the measurement procedure. TREX typically proceeds in two stages:\n"
msgstr "Yang penting, ralat ini selalunya boleh dimodelkan sebagai proses stokastik klasik yang bertindak pada hasil pengukuran. TREX memanfaatkan idea piawai daripada penyesuaian hingar: perawakan (twirling) prosedur pengukuran. TREX lazimnya berjalan dalam dua peringkat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling and classical \"untwirling\"\n"
msgstr "Twirling dan \"untwirling\" klasik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rescaling of expectation values using calibration circuits\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan semula nilai jangkaan menggunakan litar penentukuran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose an expectation value of observable $O$ is related to noisy estimates, like the following:\n"
msgstr "Andaikan nilai jangkaan observable $O$ berkaitan dengan anggaran berhingar, seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O \\rangle_\\text{ideal} \\approx a \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{meas}+b\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O \\rangle_\\text{ideal} \\approx a \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{meas}+b\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $a$ is a fixed factor that scales the estimate and $b$ is a bias from sources described above. We are using $\\approx$ here as a reminder that we are only addressing readout error here; there is still gate error to consider.\n"
msgstr "dengan $a$ ialah faktor tetap yang menskala anggaran dan $b$ ialah pincang daripada sumber yang diterangkan di atas. Kita menggunakan $\\approx$ di sini sebagai peringatan bahawa kita hanya menangani ralat bacaan di sini; masih ada ralat gate untuk dipertimbangkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Just before measurement, each qubit is randomly conjugated with a Pauli operator (like I or X). Measurement outcomes are classically untwirled afterward.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum pengukuran, setiap qubit dikonjugasi secara rawak dengan operator Pauli (seperti I atau X). Hasil pengukuran kemudiannya di-untwirl secara klasik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing how Pauli gates are used in measurement twirling.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/trex-diagram.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing how Pauli gates are used in measurement twirling.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/trex-diagram.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Averaging over these randomizations symmetrizes the readout channel. As a result, systematic asymmetries in the readout process are converted into a more symmetric error channel whose remaining effect can be treated through calibration and rescaling. In simple terms, if for example there was a bias toward the $|0\\rangle$ state, we would be missing some measurements of $|1\\rangle$. By twirling around the measurement, we randomly interchange which logical outcome is associated with the physical readout process, then undo that interchange classically afterward. Averaging over many such randomized measurements removes the systematic preference for one reported outcome over the other. This removes the dominant measurement bias under the assumptions of the TREX model, so that we have:\n"
msgstr "Pengambilan purata ke atas perawakan ini mensimetrikan saluran bacaan. Akibatnya, ketaksimetrian sistematik dalam proses bacaan ditukar kepada saluran ralat yang lebih simetri yang kesan bakinya boleh ditangani melalui penentukuran dan penskalaan semula. Secara mudah, jika sebagai contoh terdapat pincang ke arah keadaan $|0\\rangle$, kita akan kehilangan sebahagian pengukuran $|1\\rangle$. Dengan melakukan twirling di sekitar pengukuran, kita menukar secara rawak hasil logik yang dikaitkan dengan proses bacaan fizikal, kemudian membatalkan pertukaran itu secara klasik selepas itu. Mengambil purata ke atas banyak pengukuran terawak sedemikian menghapuskan keutamaan sistematik bagi satu hasil yang dilaporkan berbanding yang lain. Ini menghapuskan pincang pengukuran dominan di bawah andaian model TREX, supaya kita memperoleh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O \\rangle_\\text{ideal} \\approx a \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{twirled}+0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O \\rangle_\\text{ideal} \\approx a \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{twirled}+0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, expectation values might still need to be rescaled. The second stage is using calibration circuits (circuits with known outcomes) to estimate the scaling factor $a$. This can then be used to obtain a greatly enhanced estimate.\n"
msgstr "Walau bagaimanapun, nilai jangkaan mungkin masih perlu diskala semula. Peringkat kedua ialah menggunakan litar penentukuran (litar dengan hasil yang diketahui) untuk menganggarkan faktor penskalaan $a$. Ini kemudiannya boleh digunakan untuk mendapatkan anggaran yang jauh lebih baik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O \\rangle_\\text{ideal} \\approx \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{TREX} = a \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{twirled}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O \\rangle_\\text{ideal} \\approx \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{TREX} = a \\langle O \\rangle_\\text{twirled}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values of Pauli observables become unbiased estimators of their ideal values. No explicit noise model is learned or inverted, which is why TREX is numerically stable and inexpensive. Again, gate error has not been addressed here.\n"
msgstr "Nilai jangkaan observable Pauli menjadi penganggar tidak berat sebelah bagi nilai unggulnya. Tiada model hingar eksplisit yang dipelajari atau disongsangkan, itulah sebabnya TREX stabil secara berangka dan murah. Sekali lagi, ralat gate tidak ditangani di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the estimation of an expectation value $\\langle O\\rangle$ of observable $O$, there can be variance due to finite sampling, there can be many types of incoherent and coherent errors, and there can also be a bias, $\\delta$, due to readout error. This bias arises from sources like the asymmetric transitions we've discussed. In practice, this bias is typically well-modeled as a classical stochastic channel acting after the quantum evolution. TREX transforms the effective measurement channel so that the estimator of $\\langle O\\rangle$ is unbiased with respect to readout error. This is relatively easy to see, using the simplest example of twirling gates: X. If there is asymmetry in $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ compared to $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$, but we randomly switch which state is being read (flipping back later, classically), then this obviously removes the systematic asymmetry (though finite sampling still means there might be slight stochastic asymmetry in measurement). In practice, twirling gates for TREX are not limited to I and X, but this suffices for an explanation.\n"
msgstr "Dalam penganggaran nilai jangkaan $\\langle O\\rangle$ bagi observable $O$, boleh terdapat varians akibat persampelan terhingga, boleh terdapat banyak jenis ralat tak koheren dan koheren, dan boleh juga terdapat pincang, $\\delta$, akibat ralat bacaan. Pincang ini timbul daripada sumber seperti peralihan tak simetri yang telah kita bincangkan. Dalam praktik, pincang ini lazimnya dimodelkan dengan baik sebagai saluran stokastik klasik yang bertindak selepas evolusi kuantum. TREX mengubah saluran pengukuran berkesan supaya penganggar bagi $\\langle O\\rangle$ tidak berat sebelah terhadap ralat bacaan. Ini agak mudah dilihat, menggunakan contoh paling ringkas gate twirling: X. Jika terdapat ketaksimetrian dalam $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ berbanding $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$, tetapi kita menukar secara rawak keadaan mana yang dibaca (membalikkannya semula kemudian, secara klasik), maka ini jelas menghapuskan ketaksimetrian sistematik (walaupun persampelan terhingga masih bermakna mungkin terdapat sedikit ketaksimetrian stokastik dalam pengukuran). Dalam praktik, gate twirling untuk TREX tidak terhad kepada I dan X, tetapi ini memadai untuk penerangan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX allows us to obtain an estimate of an expectation value that is free of bias due to readout error. There could still be a bias from some other source (like coherent over-rotation); TREX targets only readout. Because TREX replaces systematic bias with randomized symmetrization, it generally converts bias into additional stochastic variance, increasing the variance of the estimator at fixed sampling cost.\n"
msgstr "TREX membolehkan kita memperoleh anggaran nilai jangkaan yang bebas daripada pincang akibat ralat bacaan. Mungkin masih ada pincang daripada sumber lain (seperti putaran berlebihan yang koheren); TREX hanya menyasarkan bacaan. Oleh kerana TREX menggantikan pincang sistematik dengan pensimetrian rawak, ia secara amnya menukar pincang kepada varians stokastik tambahan, meningkatkan varians penganggar pada kos persampelan tetap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose we use estimator on a circuit that has prepared the state $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ in the estimation of $\\langle Z\\rangle$. Suppose further that measurement errors cause outcomes corresponding to $|1\\rangle$ to be reported as $0$ 10% of the time, while outcomes corresponding to $|0\\rangle$ are reported as $1$ only 1% of the time. The asymmetry between these reporting errors introduces a measurement bias.\n"
msgstr "Andaikan kita menggunakan Estimator pada litar yang telah menyediakan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ dalam penganggaran $\\langle Z\\rangle$. Andaikan selanjutnya bahawa ralat pengukuran menyebabkan hasil yang sepadan dengan $|1\\rangle$ dilaporkan sebagai $0$ sebanyak 10% daripada masa, manakala hasil yang sepadan dengan $|0\\rangle$ dilaporkan sebagai $1$ hanya 1% daripada masa. Ketaksimetrian antara ralat pelaporan ini memperkenalkan pincang pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) In the absence of any such measurement errors, what would be the ideal expectation value of the observable $\\langle Z \\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "(a) Tanpa sebarang ralat pengukuran sedemikian, berapakah nilai jangkaan unggul bagi observable $\\langle Z \\rangle$?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(b) With the asymmetric measurement or readout errors, what is the expectation value of the observable $\\langle Z \\rangle$?\n"
msgstr "(b) Dengan ralat pengukuran atau bacaan tak simetri, berapakah nilai jangkaan bagi observable $\\langle Z \\rangle$?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c) Consider a limited set of Pauli twirling gates: I and X. Assume I and X are applied randomly with 50% probability in multiple shots. The same measurement error rates still apply. Then the Pauli gate (I or X) is undone classically. Make a table of all possible outcomes and their probabilities due to initial superposition, asymmetric measurement errors, and randomly assigned Pauli gates.\n"
msgstr "(c) Pertimbangkan set terhad gate twirling Pauli: I dan X. Andaikan I dan X digunakan secara rawak dengan kebarangkalian 50% dalam berbilang shot. Kadar ralat pengukuran yang sama masih terpakai. Kemudian gate Pauli (I atau X) dibatalkan secara klasik. Buat jadual semua hasil yang mungkin dan kebarangkalian masing-masing disebabkan superposisi awal, ralat pengukuran tak simetri, dan gate Pauli yang ditugaskan secara rawak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(d) Use the table to determine the expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle$ using the twirling strategy.\n"
msgstr "(d) Gunakan jadual itu untuk menentukan nilai jangkaan $\\langle Z \\rangle$ menggunakan strategi twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(e) Compare the expectation values: ideal, without twirling, and with twirling.\n"
msgstr "(e) Bandingkan nilai jangkaan: unggul, tanpa twirling, dan dengan twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(f) What has been omitted from this treatment that is found in a full TREX application?\n"
msgstr "(f) Apakah yang telah ditinggalkan daripada rawatan ini yang terdapat dalam aplikasi TREX penuh?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawapan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(a) You can simply use intuition and symmetry to say $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0$. To show explicitly:\n"
msgstr "(a) Anda boleh menggunakan intuisi dan simetri untuk mengatakan $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0$. Untuk menunjukkan secara eksplisit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\langle0|+\\langle1|) Z \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(\\langle0|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle0|Z|1\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}((1)\\langle0|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle0|1\\rangle+(1)\\langle1|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle1|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(1+0+0+-1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\langle0|+\\langle1|) Z \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(\\langle0|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle0|Z|1\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|0\\rangle+\\langle1|Z|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}((1)\\langle0|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle0|1\\rangle+(1)\\langle1|0\\rangle+(-1)\\langle1|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2}(1+0+0+-1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(b) The state could collapse to either $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ when measured, each with 50% chance. But of the 50% that collapse to the $|0\\rangle$ state, 1% of those (or 0.5% of all cases) will be mis-reported as $|1\\rangle$. Of the 50% that collapse to $|1\\rangle$, 10% (or 5% of all cases) will be mis-reported as $|0\\rangle$. This leaves us with:\n"
"* $|0\\rangle$ 54.5%\n"
"* $|1\\rangle$ 45.5%\n"
"Ignoring all other types of possible errors, we would obtain an estimate of\n"
msgstr ""
"(b) Keadaan boleh runtuh kepada $|0\\rangle$ atau $|1\\rangle$ apabila diukur, masing-masing dengan peluang 50%. Tetapi daripada 50% yang runtuh kepada keadaan $|0\\rangle$, 1% daripadanya (atau 0.5% daripada semua kes) akan tersalah dilaporkan sebagai $|1\\rangle$. Daripada 50% yang runtuh kepada $|1\\rangle$, 10% (atau 5% daripada semua kes) akan tersalah dilaporkan sebagai $|0\\rangle$. Ini meninggalkan kita dengan:\n"
"* $|0\\rangle$ 54.5%\n"
"* $|1\\rangle$ 45.5%\n"
"Tanpa mengambil kira semua jenis ralat lain yang mungkin, kita akan memperoleh anggaran\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle = (0.545)(1)+(0.455)(-1) = 0.09\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle = (0.545)(1)+(0.455)(-1) = 0.09\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(c)\n"
msgstr "(c)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Pauli | Ideal measurement outcome | Outcome after Pauli | Readout error | Undo Pauli | Final reported outcome | Probability |\n"
"|--------------|---------|----------|-------------|------------|------------|------------|\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | None | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | None | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | None | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | None | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Pauli | Hasil pengukuran unggul | Hasil selepas Pauli | Ralat bacaan | Batalkan Pauli | Hasil akhir dilaporkan | Kebarangkalian |\n"
"|--------------|---------|----------|-------------|------------|------------|------------|\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | Tiada | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| I | 0 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | Tiada | I | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| I | 1 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | I | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | Tiada | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 90% = 22.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 0 | 1 | $1 \\rightarrow 0$ | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 10% = 2.5\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | Tiada | X | 1 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 99% = 24.75\\% |\n"
"| X | 1 | 0 | $0 \\rightarrow 1$ | X | 0 | 50\\% $\\times$ 50\\% $\\times$ 1% = 0.25\\% |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(d) From previous parts, we know the expectation values of Z in each of the final states. We need only take the weighted average:\n"
msgstr "(d) Daripada bahagian sebelumnya, kita tahu nilai jangkaan Z dalam setiap keadaan akhir. Kita hanya perlu mengambil purata berpemberat:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = (0.2475)(1)+(0.0025)(-1)+(0.225)(-1)+(0.025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& + (0.225)(1)+(0.025)(-1)+(0.2475)(-1)+(0.0025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = (0.2475)(1)+(0.0025)(-1)+(0.225)(-1)+(0.025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& + (0.225)(1)+(0.025)(-1)+(0.2475)(-1)+(0.0025)(1)\\\\\n"
"& = 0\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(e) In this very simple case our application of twirling recovered exactly the ideal expectation value. That is not typical. What is typical is that the twirling undoes biases like those introduced through asymmetric transitions, and returns an expectation value closer to the ideal.\n"
msgstr "(e) Dalam kes yang sangat ringkas ini, penggunaan twirling kita memulihkan dengan tepat nilai jangkaan unggul. Itu bukan perkara lazim. Yang lazim ialah twirling membatalkan pincang seperti yang diperkenalkan melalui peralihan tak simetri, dan mengembalikan nilai jangkaan yang lebih dekat dengan nilai unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(f) This is a toy model application. There could be several things missing. Notably, we have not run calibration circuits here to estimate a rescaling factor $a$. This is typically necessary.\n"
msgstr "(f) Ini ialah aplikasi model mainan. Mungkin ada beberapa perkara yang tiada. Terutamanya, kita tidak menjalankan litar penentukuran di sini untuk menganggarkan faktor penskalaan semula $a$. Ini lazimnya diperlukan.\n"

