# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation details {#implementation-details}"
msgstr "Butiran pelaksanaan {#implementation-details}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX is automatically applied when using the EstimatorV2 primitive with `resilience_level = 1` (the default). Note that it is **not** applied automatically to the Sampler primitive, because Sampler returns full probability distributions rather than expectation values.\n"
msgstr "TREX digunakan secara automatik apabila menggunakan primitif EstimatorV2 dengan `resilience_level = 1` (lalai). Perhatikan bahawa ia **tidak** digunakan secara automatik pada primitif Sampler, kerana Sampler mengembalikan taburan kebarangkalian penuh dan bukannya nilai jangkaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When TREX is enabled, the runtime generates measurement-twirled circuit variants by inserting random single-qubit Paulis immediately before measurement. Classical post-processing reverses these Paulis. These circuit variants are random across different shots and also across different qubits within a shot. All circuit variants are then combined into a single estimator.\n"
msgstr "Apabila TREX didayakan, runtime menjana varian litar terpilin-pengukuran dengan menyisipkan Pauli satu-qubit rawak sejurus sebelum pengukuran. Pasca-pemprosesan klasik membalikkan Pauli ini. Varian litar ini adalah rawak merentasi shot yang berbeza dan juga merentasi qubit yang berbeza dalam satu shot. Semua varian litar kemudiannya digabungkan menjadi satu penganggar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TREX is very scalable. It requires additional calibration circuits, such that the sampling overhead is typically a small constant factor (often 2-4x).\n"
"But the mitigation is observable-specific, not distribution-preserving.\n"
msgstr ""
"TREX sangat berskala. Ia memerlukan litar penentukuran tambahan, sehingga overhed persampelan lazimnya faktor tetap yang kecil (selalunya 2-4x).\n"
"Tetapi pengurangan itu khusus observable, bukan mengekalkan taburan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX is designed to integrate cleanly with many error suppression and error mitigation methods, including the following:\n"
msgstr "TREX direka untuk disepadukan dengan baik bersama banyak kaedah penindasan ralat dan pengurangan ralat, termasuk yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling (DD) - acts during idle times, orthogonal to readout mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Dynamical decoupling (DD) - bertindak semasa masa melahu, ortogon kepada pengurangan bacaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gate or Pauli twirling - often complementary; TREX already relies on twirling but targets only readout noise.\n"
msgstr "Gate atau Pauli twirling - selalunya saling melengkapi; TREX sudah bergantung pada twirling tetapi hanya menyasarkan hingar bacaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-Noise Extrapolation (ZNE) - ZNE targets gate noise, while TREX handles measurement bias. This combination is used at resilience level 2.\n"
msgstr "Zero-Noise Extrapolation (ZNE) - ZNE menyasarkan hingar gate, manakala TREX menangani pincang pengukuran. Gabungan ini digunakan pada tahap daya tahan 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error amplification and probabilistic error cancellation in Estimator workflows.\n"
msgstr "Penguatan ralat probabilistik dan pembatalan ralat probabilistik dalam aliran kerja Estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, some methods cannot (or should not) be combined with TREX:\n"
msgstr "Walau bagaimanapun, sesetengah kaedah tidak boleh (atau tidak sepatutnya) digabungkan dengan TREX:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampler-level probability correction: TREX does not return corrected bitstring probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Pembetulan kebarangkalian peringkat Sampler: TREX tidak mengembalikan kebarangkalian rentetan bit yang dibetulkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-hoc mitigation on already-mitigated TREX data: double correction can reintroduce bias.\n"
msgstr "Pengurangan post-hoc pada data TREX yang sudah dikurangkan: pembetulan berganda boleh memperkenalkan semula pincang.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining TREX with assignment-matrix-based readout mitigation like M3 is tricky. M3 assumes a fixed measurement channel. TREX deliberately randomizes measurement, invalidating assumption used by M3. In that sense, you cannot simply combine these techniques. However, if you apply measurement twirling during the calibration used in M3, you might be able to leverage both an assignment matrix-like approach and a twirling mitigation approach simultaneously (though this twirling approach is not quite the same as TREX). This is a recurring theme in combining mitigation and suppression techniques: blindly adding techniques fails; adding them carefully such that they are \"aware\" of each other can work and can be highly beneficial.\n"
msgstr "Menggabungkan TREX dengan pengurangan bacaan berasaskan matriks penugasan seperti M3 adalah rumit. M3 mengandaikan saluran pengukuran yang tetap. TREX sengaja merawakkan pengukuran, sekali gus membatalkan andaian yang digunakan oleh M3. Dalam erti kata itu, anda tidak boleh sekadar menggabungkan teknik-teknik ini. Namun, jika anda menggunakan twirling pengukuran semasa penentukuran yang digunakan dalam M3, anda mungkin dapat memanfaatkan pendekatan seakan-akan matriks penugasan dan pendekatan pengurangan twirling secara serentak (walaupun pendekatan twirling ini tidak sama sepenuhnya dengan TREX). Ini ialah tema yang berulang dalam menggabungkan teknik pengurangan dan penindasan: menambah teknik secara membuta tuli akan gagal; menambahnya dengan teliti supaya teknik-teknik itu \"sedar\" akan satu sama lain boleh berjaya dan amat bermanfaat.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX only guarantees expectation values that are free of bias due to readout errors; it does not reduce variance, nor does it protect against other types of bias. It certainly does not correct all errors. However, it is often a substantial improvement, and it is achievable with much lower overhead than some other methods that require learning full noise models. TREX is often the lowest-cost and most robust readout mitigation available, making it an excellent default in experiments.\n"
msgstr "TREX hanya menjamin nilai jangkaan yang bebas daripada pincang akibat ralat bacaan; ia tidak mengurangkan varians, dan tidak melindungi daripada jenis pincang lain. Ia sudah tentu tidak membetulkan semua ralat. Namun, ia sering merupakan peningkatan yang ketara, dan boleh dicapai dengan overhed yang jauh lebih rendah daripada beberapa kaedah lain yang memerlukan pembelajaran model hingar penuh. TREX selalunya pengurangan bacaan yang paling murah dan paling teguh yang tersedia, menjadikannya lalai yang sangat baik dalam eksperimen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX with Qiskit {#trex-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "TREX dengan Qiskit {#trex-with-qiskit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we create a simple two-qubit circuit, and use Estimator to estimate the expectation value of a very simple observable, `ZX`. The ideal expectation value is 1. We will compare the expectation values with and without TREX.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita mencipta litar dua qubit yang ringkas, dan menggunakan Estimator untuk menganggarkan nilai jangkaan bagi satu observabel yang sangat ringkas, `ZX`. Nilai jangkaan unggul ialah 1. Kita akan membandingkan nilai jangkaan dengan dan tanpa TREX.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the simple quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Cipta litar kuantum yang ringkas.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/46c98dd4-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/46c98dd4-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit using a pass manager.\n"
msgstr "Transpile litar menggunakan pass manager.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the same layout from transpilation to the observable.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan susun atur yang sama daripada transpilation pada observabel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the experiment on a real quantum computer. First we proceed with `reslience_level = 1`; this is the default, but we have made it explicit for distinguishing the two cases.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan eksperimen pada komputer kuantum sebenar. Mula-mula kita teruskan dengan `reslience_level = 1`; ini ialah nilai lalai, tetapi kita menyatakannya secara eksplisit untuk membezakan kedua-dua kes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we set the `resilience_level` to 0 to run without TREX.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita tetapkan `resilience_level` kepada 0 untuk menjalankan tanpa TREX.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The expectation value is substantially closer to the ideal (1) with TREX, as expected.\n"
"Of course, this was a single expectation value on a single qubit. We now prepare a circuit using non-Clifford gates and many qubits to test whether the TREX improvement remains robust in a different setting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai jangkaan jauh lebih hampir dengan nilai unggul (1) dengan TREX, seperti yang dijangkakan.\n"
"Tentu sekali, ini ialah satu nilai jangkaan pada satu qubit. Sekarang kita menyediakan litar menggunakan get bukan Clifford dan banyak qubit untuk menguji sama ada peningkatan TREX kekal teguh dalam keadaan yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, there is nothing special about the rotation angle $7\\pi/8$. We simply chose any unequal superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ in order to probe effects of asymmetric erroneous transitions and how they are treated by TREX. Given this state, the ideal expectation value of Z on every qubit, in the absence of any errors (readout or otherwise) would be:\n"
msgstr "Di sini, tiada apa-apa yang istimewa tentang sudut putaran $7\\pi/8$. Kita sekadar memilih mana-mana superposisi tidak sama rata bagi $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ untuk mengkaji kesan peralihan ralat tidak simetri dan cara ia dikendalikan oleh TREX. Dengan keadaan ini, nilai jangkaan unggul bagi Z pada setiap qubit, tanpa sebarang ralat (bacaan atau lain-lain) ialah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle = \\langle \\psi |Z|\\psi \\rangle = -0.9239\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle = \\langle \\psi |Z|\\psi \\rangle = -0.9239\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We therefore hope to obtain expectation values close to -0.924 on all qubits. We will see if TREX improves each expectation value individually and also whether it improves the average over all qubits.\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, kita berharap memperoleh nilai jangkaan yang hampir dengan -0.924 pada semua qubit. Kita akan lihat sama ada TREX memperbaiki setiap nilai jangkaan secara individu dan juga sama ada ia memperbaiki purata bagi semua qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the expectation value above through direct calculation.\n"
msgstr "Sahkan nilai jangkaan di atas melalui pengiraan langsung.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi |Z|\\psi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle 0 |RX^\\dagger (7\\pi/8) \\quad Z \\quad RX(7\\pi/8)|0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -2\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& = \\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = -0.9239...\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi |Z|\\psi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle 0 |RX^\\dagger (7\\pi/8) \\quad Z \\quad RX(7\\pi/8)|0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) & \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -i\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right) \\\\ -2\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& = \\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{16}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = -0.9239...\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We transpile using a pass manager.\n"
msgstr "Kita melakukan transpile menggunakan pass manager.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we construct one observable per qubit so that we can estimate all twenty $\\langle Z_i\\rangle$ expectation values in a single workflow. That is, for the $i^\\text{th}$ qubit, we want an observable with all identities $I$, except at the $i^\\text{th}$ position, where we want a $Z$. Remember to apply your transpiled layout to your observables as well.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita membina satu observabel bagi setiap qubit supaya kita dapat menganggarkan kesemua dua puluh nilai jangkaan $\\langle Z_i\\rangle$ dalam satu aliran kerja. Maksudnya, bagi qubit ke-$i^\\text{th}$, kita mahu observabel dengan semua identiti $I$, kecuali pada kedudukan ke-$i^\\text{th}$, di mana kita mahu $Z$. Ingat untuk menggunakan susun atur hasil transpile anda pada observabel anda juga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can execute. The code cell below uses [session mode](/guides/run-jobs-session); if you do not have access to sessions, you can replace it with [batch mode](/guides/run-jobs-batch) to run the same workflow but with possible queue times between circuits.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita boleh melaksanakan. Sel kod di bawah menggunakan [session mode](/guides/run-jobs-session); jika anda tidak mempunyai akses kepada session, anda boleh menggantikannya dengan [batch mode](/guides/run-jobs-batch) untuk menjalankan aliran kerja yang sama tetapi dengan kemungkinan masa giliran antara litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we compare the mean absolute errors with and without TREX.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita membandingkan ralat mutlak purata dengan dan tanpa TREX.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/03aff38d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/03aff38d-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREX certainly appears to have helped. The expectation value on every qubit has improved, with the sole exception of qubit 16. Such an outlier is to be expected. We can quantify the overall application of TREX to the circuit by taking the average values.\n"
msgstr "TREX nyata telah membantu. Nilai jangkaan pada setiap qubit telah bertambah baik, kecuali qubit 16. Nilai terpencil sedemikian memang dijangka. Kita boleh mengukur kesan keseluruhan TREX pada litar dengan mengambil nilai purata.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On average, TREX moved our results about 2.9% closer to the ideal results, and left us with a result that is, on average, different from the theoretical ideal by just 0.4%. This is great, and this low-overhead improvement is exactly why TREX is the default error mitigation on Estimator. But we must once more emphasize that TREX is removing a bias in readout error, not correcting all our errors. We chose an initial state that had a good chance of being affected by asymmetry in readout. The effect would have been different if we had prepared each qubit in a different state. For a trivial argument why this must be the case, consider what would happen if we left each qubit in the ground state $|0\\rangle$. There would be no opportunity to observe (or correct) an asymmetry in readout error between the states $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Secara purata, TREX menggerakkan keputusan kita kira-kira 2.9% lebih dekat dengan keputusan unggul, dan meninggalkan kita dengan keputusan yang, secara purata, berbeza daripada nilai unggul teori hanya 0.4%. Ini bagus, dan peningkatan beroverhed rendah inilah sebabnya TREX ialah pengurangan ralat lalai pada Estimator. Namun kita sekali lagi mesti menekankan bahawa TREX menghapuskan pincang dalam ralat bacaan, bukan membetulkan semua ralat kita. Kita memilih keadaan awal yang berkemungkinan besar terjejas oleh asimetri dalam bacaan. Kesannya akan berbeza jika kita menyediakan setiap qubit dalam keadaan yang berlainan. Sebagai hujah mudah mengapa ini mesti benar, pertimbangkan apa yang akan berlaku jika kita membiarkan setiap qubit dalam keadaan asas $|0\\rangle$. Tiada peluang untuk memerhati (atau membetulkan) asimetri dalam ralat bacaan antara keadaan $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi hingar sifar (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is one of the most widely used error-mitigation techniques. The general strategy is also easy to understand, though the details of its implementation are complex. ZNE works by:\n"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi hingar sifar (ZNE) ialah salah satu teknik pengurangan ralat yang paling meluas digunakan. Strategi amnya juga mudah difahami, walaupun butiran pelaksanaannya kompleks. ZNE berfungsi dengan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running a target circuit at multiple \"noise levels\" &mdash; modifications to the circuit that cause its noise to scale in predictable ways\n"
msgstr "Menjalankan litar sasaran pada beberapa \"tahap hingar\" &mdash; pengubahsuaian pada litar yang menyebabkan hingarnya berskala dengan cara yang boleh diramal\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimating the observable of interest for each noise scale.\n"
msgstr "Menganggarkan observabel yang diminati bagi setiap skala hingar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extrapolating back to zero noise using a fitting model (linear, polynomial, exponential, and so on).\n"
msgstr "Mengekstrapolasi kembali kepada hingar sifar menggunakan model penyuaian (linear, polinomial, eksponen, dan sebagainya).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result is an estimate of what the observable would have been in the zero-noise limit implied by the extrapolation model.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya ialah anggaran tentang nilai observabel itu dalam had hingar sifar yang tersirat oleh model ekstrapolasi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing many expectation values at many noise levels. These results lie approximately on a line, and the best fit line is traced backwards to the zero-noise case. This is zero noise extrapolation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/zne.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram showing many expectation values at many noise levels. These results lie approximately on a line, and the best fit line is traced backwards to the zero-noise case. This is zero noise extrapolation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/zne.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE does not guarantee that noise increases smoothly or linearly as we modify circuits. Instead, it **assumes** that noise scaling is sufficiently well-behaved to allow extrapolation. The complexity in ZNE is in how one modifies circuits to satisfy this assumption as well as possible. We will examine some approaches in this lesson.\n"
msgstr "ZNE tidak menjamin bahawa hingar meningkat secara lancar atau linear apabila kita mengubah suai litar. Sebaliknya, ia **mengandaikan** bahawa penskalaan hingar berkelakuan cukup baik untuk membenarkan ekstrapolasi. Kerumitan dalam ZNE terletak pada cara seseorang mengubah suai litar untuk memenuhi andaian ini sebaik mungkin. Kita akan meneliti beberapa pendekatan dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE resource scaling {#zne-resource-scaling}"
msgstr "Penskalaan sumber ZNE {#zne-resource-scaling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In ZNE, the overhead is mostly quantum overhead. That is, to obtain expectation values at $k$ noise levels, you have to carry out your experiment on $k$ circuits, each with many shots. To maintain a fixed statistical precision, the total number of samples generally increases as additional noise-scaled circuits are introduced.\n"
msgstr "Dalam ZNE, overhed kebanyakannya ialah overhed kuantum. Maksudnya, untuk memperoleh nilai jangkaan pada $k$ tahap hingar, anda perlu menjalankan eksperimen anda pada $k$ litar, masing-masing dengan banyak shot. Untuk mengekalkan ketepatan statistik yang tetap, jumlah sampel secara amnya meningkat apabila litar berskala hingar tambahan diperkenalkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of noise levels you examine, $k$, will depend on the method used to scale the noise. For one simple noise-scaling technique (called \"gate-folding\", discussed below), $k$ is commonly between 3 and 5. A different method (probabilistic noise amplification (PNA)) allows for non-integer noise factors, and typically results in lower noise levels than gate-folding. The total overhead scales roughly as:\n"
msgstr "Bilangan tahap hingar yang anda kaji, $k$, bergantung pada kaedah yang digunakan untuk menskalakan hingar. Bagi satu teknik penskalaan hingar yang ringkas (dipanggil \"gate-folding\", dibincangkan di bawah), $k$ lazimnya antara 3 dan 5. Kaedah yang berbeza (penguatan hingar kebarangkalian (PNA)) membenarkan faktor hingar bukan integer, dan lazimnya menghasilkan tahap hingar yang lebih rendah daripada gate-folding. Jumlah overhed berskala kira-kira sebagai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{Runtime} \\sim k \\cdot S\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{Runtime} \\sim k \\cdot S\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $S$ is the baseline shot count. Another thing to keep in mind is that if noise scaling involves repeated gates, the circuit depth might increase by a factor proportional to the noise-scaling value. The scaling of noise that comes with increased depth is the point, but keep the total depth in mind.\n"
msgstr "di mana $S$ ialah bilangan shot asas. Satu lagi perkara yang perlu diingat ialah jika penskalaan hingar melibatkan get yang diulang, kedalaman litar mungkin meningkat dengan faktor yang berkadar dengan nilai penskalaan hingar. Penskalaan hingar yang datang bersama pertambahan kedalaman memang menjadi tujuannya, tetapi ingat jumlah kedalaman.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE is well-suited to problems in which the following points apply:\n"
msgstr "ZNE sesuai untuk masalah di mana perkara berikut terpakai:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You need a general-purpose mitigation method effective on many error types.\n"
msgstr "Anda memerlukan kaedah pengurangan serba guna yang berkesan pada banyak jenis ralat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit depth is not too large; ZNE fails when the scaled circuit becomes too noisy to extrapolate.\n"
msgstr "Kedalaman litar tidak terlalu besar; ZNE gagal apabila litar berskala menjadi terlalu bising untuk diekstrapolasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can tolerate moderate runtime overhead for improved accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh menerima overhed masa jalan yang sederhana demi ketepatan yang lebih baik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice this makes ZNE ideal for many variational circuits, expectation-value estimation, and other near-term quantum algorithms. It is implemented in Estimator using `resilience_level = 2`. Note that ZNE extrapolates in a space that has a single outcome as a function of noise throughout the circuit. That means it is amenable to estimation problems, but not to sampling problems. It is not designed to work on distributions of bitstrings.\n"
msgstr "Dalam praktik, ini menjadikan ZNE sesuai untuk banyak litar variasi, penganggaran nilai jangkaan, dan algoritma kuantum jangka dekat yang lain. Ia dilaksanakan dalam Estimator menggunakan `resilience_level = 2`. Perhatikan bahawa ZNE mengekstrapolasi dalam ruang yang mempunyai satu hasil tunggal sebagai fungsi hingar di seluruh litar. Ini bermakna ia sesuai untuk masalah penganggaran, tetapi tidak untuk masalah persampelan. Ia tidak direka untuk berfungsi pada taburan rentetan bit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise factors {#noise-factors}"
msgstr "Faktor hingar {#noise-factors}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "How exactly can we increase the level of noise in a circuit? There are two main ways, although many variants exist.\n"
msgstr "Bagaimanakah sebenarnya kita boleh meningkatkan tahap hingar dalam litar? Terdapat dua cara utama, walaupun banyak variasi wujud.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace a gate or block of gates $G$ with $GG^\\dagger G$. Because gates on quantum computers are unitary, we know that $G^\\dagger = G^{-1}$ so that logically: $GG^\\dagger G = G$. However, every repetition of $G$ or $G^\\dagger$ adds similar or identical error, allowing us to scale up noise/error levels. Note that the replacement shown above takes us from the original noise of gate $G$ (noise level 1) to three times that noise level in $GG^\\dagger G$ (noise level 3). In practice, we can repeat the last two gates $\\ell$ times: $G(G^\\dagger G)^\\ell$ to obtain a noise level $2\\ell+1$. This is called **gate folding**, and it is a very common noise scaling technique.\n"
msgstr "Gantikan get atau blok get $G$ dengan $GG^\\dagger G$. Oleh kerana get pada komputer kuantum adalah uniter, kita tahu bahawa $G^\\dagger = G^{-1}$ supaya secara logik: $GG^\\dagger G = G$. Namun, setiap pengulangan $G$ atau $G^\\dagger$ menambah ralat yang serupa atau sama, membolehkan kita menaikkan tahap hingar/ralat. Perhatikan bahawa penggantian yang ditunjukkan di atas membawa kita daripada hingar asal get $G$ (tahap hingar 1) kepada tiga kali ganda tahap hingar itu dalam $GG^\\dagger G$ (tahap hingar 3). Dalam praktik, kita boleh mengulang dua get terakhir sebanyak $\\ell$ kali: $G(G^\\dagger G)^\\ell$ untuk memperoleh tahap hingar $2\\ell+1$. Ini dipanggil **gate folding**, dan ia ialah teknik penskalaan hingar yang sangat lazim.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are other methods for increasing the noise level, such as probabilistic error amplification (PEA). In PEA, we first learn a suitable noise model for the circuit, typically expressed as a Pauli channel. Noise is then amplified by sampling from a rescaled version of this learned noise channel. By adjusting the sampling, you can continuously scale the effective noise strength, including to non-integer values.\n"
msgstr "Terdapat kaedah lain untuk meningkatkan tahap hingar, seperti penguatan ralat kebarangkalian (PEA). Dalam PEA, kita mula-mula mempelajari model hingar yang sesuai untuk litar, lazimnya dinyatakan sebagai saluran Pauli. Hingar kemudian dikuatkan dengan membuat persampelan daripada versi saluran hingar yang telah dipelajari ini yang diskalakan semula. Dengan melaraskan persampelan, anda boleh menskalakan kekuatan hingar berkesan secara berterusan, termasuk kepada nilai bukan integer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, gate folding can very reliably scale errors, but it can also lead to very deep circuits. If you only need three noise levels (1, 3, and 5), it means increasing your circuit depth by a factor of 5 and still obtaining reasonable results. Thus, if your target circuit has a transpiled, two-qubit depth of 60 or more, PEA is likely a better fit than gate-folding.\n"
msgstr "Dalam praktik, gate folding boleh menskalakan ralat dengan sangat boleh dipercayai, tetapi ia juga boleh menghasilkan litar yang sangat dalam. Jika anda hanya memerlukan tiga tahap hingar (1, 3, dan 5), ini bermakna meningkatkan kedalaman litar anda dengan faktor 5 dan masih memperoleh keputusan yang munasabah. Oleh itu, jika litar sasaran anda mempunyai kedalaman dua qubit hasil transpile sebanyak 60 atau lebih, PEA berkemungkinan lebih sesuai daripada gate-folding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gates can be folded either locally (meaning you repeat $GG^\\dagger G$ for each two-qubit gate as soon as it occurs), or they can be grouped into a block of gates and the block can be repeated (like gates $ABC\\rightarrow ABC(ABC)^\\dagger ABC$). Often local folding is preferable for assumptions made by ZNE, but both are possible.\n"
msgstr "Get boleh dilipat sama ada secara setempat (bermaksud anda mengulang $GG^\\dagger G$ bagi setiap get dua qubit sebaik sahaja ia berlaku), atau ia boleh dikumpulkan menjadi blok get dan blok itu diulang (seperti get $ABC\\rightarrow ABC(ABC)^\\dagger ABC$). Lipatan setempat sering lebih baik bagi andaian yang dibuat oleh ZNE, tetapi kedua-duanya boleh dilakukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A lot of nuance goes into the statistical treatment of noise-scaled results in ZNE. For example, at five times the noise level your results are certain to have higher variance and be less reliable. Should that be treated with the same weight as lower-noise data points? No. However, for the purposes of seeing ZNE in action, we will ignore some of this complexity for a toy model experiment, in which we will build folded circuits by hand, and do a naive extrapolation with equal weightings to illustrate the key steps. But we will follow this with an experiment using the ZNE functionality built into Qiskit, and we will see that it does a substantially better job of handling the complexity we are skipping.\n"
msgstr "Banyak nuansa terlibat dalam rawatan statistik keputusan berskala hingar dalam ZNE. Contohnya, pada lima kali ganda tahap hingar, keputusan anda pasti mempunyai varians yang lebih tinggi dan kurang boleh dipercayai. Patutkah ia diberi pemberat yang sama seperti titik data berhingar rendah? Tidak. Namun, bagi tujuan melihat ZNE berfungsi, kita akan mengabaikan sebahagian kerumitan ini untuk eksperimen model mainan, di mana kita akan membina litar terlipat secara manual, dan melakukan ekstrapolasi naif dengan pemberat sama rata untuk menggambarkan langkah-langkah utama. Tetapi kita akan menyusulinya dengan eksperimen menggunakan fungsi ZNE terbina dalam Qiskit, dan kita akan melihat bahawa ia mengendalikan kerumitan yang kita langkau dengan jauh lebih baik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE by hand {#zne-by-hand}"
msgstr "ZNE secara manual {#zne-by-hand}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We start by selecting a quantum circuit and an observable for which we can calculate the ideal expectation value in the absence of noise and errors. We choose a GHZ state $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}+|1\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\\right)$, with an even number of qubits. Our observable is $Z^{\\otimes N}$. We choose this for a number of reasons:\n"
"* The expectation value $\\langle Z^{\\otimes N}\\rangle = 1$ is trivial to calculate in the ideal case. Because the number of qubits is even, we either get a `1` from every $Z$, multiplied together, or we get a `-1` from every $Z$, multiplied together an even number of times.\n"
"* This will be fairly sensitive to errors and noise, since a single error on one qubit can flip the overall outcome from that shot from +1 to -1.\n"
"* The expectation value is far from 0. ZNE can encounter difficulties when the ideal expectation value is very near zero, because high noise levels will tend to randomize outcomes, making them positive as often as negative. The result is that high noise values will end up yielding values close to the ideal; this can make extrapolation very tricky.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bermula dengan memilih litar kuantum dan observable yang nilai jangkaan unggulnya boleh dikira tanpa hingar dan ralat. Kita memilih keadaan GHZ $|\\psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}+|1\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\\right)$, dengan bilangan qubit genap. Observable kita ialah $Z^{\\otimes N}$. Kita memilih ini atas beberapa sebab:\n"
"* Nilai jangkaan $\\langle Z^{\\otimes N}\\rangle = 1$ mudah dikira dalam kes unggul. Oleh kerana bilangan qubit genap, kita mendapat `1` daripada setiap $Z$, didarab bersama, atau kita mendapat `-1` daripada setiap $Z$, didarab bersama sebanyak bilangan genap kali.\n"
"* Ini agak sensitif kepada ralat dan hingar, kerana satu ralat pada satu qubit boleh membalikkan hasil keseluruhan shot itu daripada +1 kepada -1.\n"
"* Nilai jangkaan jauh daripada 0. ZNE boleh menghadapi kesukaran apabila nilai jangkaan unggul sangat hampir kepada sifar, kerana tahap hingar yang tinggi cenderung merawakkan hasil, menjadikannya positif sama kerap dengan negatif. Akibatnya, nilai hingar yang tinggi akan menghasilkan nilai yang hampir dengan nilai unggul; ini boleh menjadikan ekstrapolasi sangat rumit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this motivation in mind, let's build our circuits.\n"
msgstr "Dengan motivasi ini dalam fikiran, mari kita bina litar kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note the subtlety that here $\\text{CNOT}^{-1} = \\text{CNOT}^\\dagger = \\text{CNOT}$. Even though gate folding was advertised as consisting of operators of the form $GG^\\dagger G$, here that same structure looks like CNOT CNOT CNOT.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan kehalusan bahawa di sini $\\text{CNOT}^{-1} = \\text{CNOT}^\\dagger = \\text{CNOT}$. Walaupun gate folding diperkenalkan sebagai terdiri daripada operator berbentuk $GG^\\dagger G$, di sini struktur yang sama kelihatan seperti CNOT CNOT CNOT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's make sure that our $0^\\text{th}$ circuit is indeed the normal GHZ circuit:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita pastikan litar ke-$0^\\text{th}$ kita memang litar GHZ biasa:\n"

