msgstr "Anda boleh melihat litar-litar lain untuk mengesahkan bahawa ia mempunyai struktur yang dijangka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we build our observables.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita membina observabel kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We build a pass manager and apply it to our circuits. We then take the layouts and apply them to our observables.\n"
msgstr "Kita membina pass manager dan menggunakannya pada litar kita. Kemudian kita mengambil susun atur dan menggunakannya pada observabel kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Format the `pubs`.\n"
msgstr "Format `pubs`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we run Estimator. We would like to focus on the role of ZNE, and so we might want to set `resilience_level = 0` to avoid conflating effects of twirling with the effect of ZNE. However, we also want to compare our \"by-hand\" ZNE to the ZNE settings built into Qiskit, which include twirling. We thus set `resilience_level = 1` here. Setting `resilience_level = 2` invokes the Qiskit ZNE settings, which we will use shortly.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita menjalankan Estimator. Kita ingin menumpukan pada peranan ZNE, jadi kita mungkin mahu menetapkan `resilience_level = 0` untuk mengelakkan kesan twirling bercampur dengan kesan ZNE. Namun, kita juga mahu membandingkan ZNE \"secara manual\" kita dengan tetapan ZNE terbina dalam Qiskit, yang termasuk twirling. Oleh itu kita menetapkan `resilience_level = 1` di sini. Menetapkan `resilience_level = 2` mengaktifkan tetapan ZNE Qiskit, yang akan kita gunakan sebentar lagi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we print out the noise levels and expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita mencetak tahap hingar dan nilai jangkaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the part where we are being the most cavalier: we do a linear fit to these data without any attention being paid to the variance of each value we obtained, and without trying to theoretically predict whether the fit needs to be linear. Again, the built-in ZNE does a much better job than what we're doing by hand.\n"
msgstr "Inilah bahagian di mana kita paling ambil mudah: kita melakukan penyuaian linear pada data ini tanpa memberi perhatian kepada varians setiap nilai yang kita peroleh, dan tanpa cuba meramal secara teori sama ada penyuaian itu perlu linear. Sekali lagi, ZNE terbina dalam melakukan kerja yang jauh lebih baik daripada apa yang kita lakukan secara manual.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We go ahead and plot this prior to interpretation.\n"
msgstr "Kita teruskan dengan memplot ini sebelum membuat tafsiran.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/a5b5bdec-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/a5b5bdec-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the making of this lesson, from the extrapolation to the zero-noise case, we get an expectation value of 0.959. Your values might differ. This is substantially better than the raw circuit's expectation value of 0.83, around 13% closer to the ideal value. But you can also see that we are using one data point where the expectation value was down at 0.31. Obviously this data point is of poorer quality. If that data point had been given lower weighting in our linear approximation, and the line were fitted more to the first two data points, we can see the zero-extrapolated estimate would have been higher (nearer the ideal value). This sort of consideration is handled automatically in the ZNE built into Estimator.\n"
msgstr "Semasa pelajaran ini dibuat, daripada ekstrapolasi kepada kes hingar sifar, kita memperoleh nilai jangkaan 0.959. Nilai anda mungkin berbeza. Ini jauh lebih baik daripada nilai jangkaan litar mentah iaitu 0.83, kira-kira 13% lebih hampir dengan nilai unggul. Tetapi anda juga dapat melihat bahawa kita menggunakan satu titik data di mana nilai jangkaan jatuh pada 0.31. Jelas sekali titik data ini berkualiti lebih rendah. Jika titik data itu diberi pemberat lebih rendah dalam penghampiran linear kita, dan garis itu disuaikan lebih kepada dua titik data pertama, kita dapat melihat anggaran ekstrapolasi sifar akan lebih tinggi (lebih dekat dengan nilai unggul). Pertimbangan seperti ini dikendalikan secara automatik dalam ZNE terbina dalam Estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE built into Estimator {#zne-built-into-estimator}"
msgstr "ZNE terbina dalam Estimator {#zne-built-into-estimator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's see what happens when we use the ZNE functionality built into Estimator. We start by defining a simple GHZ circuit, without any gate folding.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita lihat apa yang berlaku apabila kita menggunakan fungsi ZNE terbina dalam Estimator. Kita bermula dengan mentakrifkan litar GHZ yang ringkas, tanpa sebarang gate folding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We define the same observable as before.\n"
msgstr "Kita mentakrifkan observabel yang sama seperti sebelum ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We once again define a pass manager, using `optimization_level = 1`. We will return to this choice below.\n"
msgstr "Kita sekali lagi mentakrifkan pass manager, menggunakan `optimization_level = 1`. Kita akan kembali kepada pilihan ini di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the circuit and apply the layout to the observables.\n"
msgstr "Lakukan transpile pada litar dan gunakan susun atur pada observabel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We run the Estimator using ZNE and twirling, and we compare the outcomes to our ZNE by-hand implementation. In particular, we compare them to the result without ZNE (`value_no_zne`).\n"
msgstr "Kita menjalankan Estimator menggunakan ZNE dan twirling, dan kita membandingkan hasilnya dengan pelaksanaan ZNE secara manual kita. Khususnya, kita membandingkannya dengan keputusan tanpa ZNE (`value_no_zne`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can retrieve the values at each noise factor using the syntax `job_zne.result()[0].data.evs_noise_factors`. As before, we could naively use these results to get a linear fit and extrapolate to the zero-noise case, but the estimator with `resilience_level = 2` has already done a better job, taking variance and other considerations into account. Below we show what a linear extrapolation would yield, and we show what built-in ZNE actually yielded.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh mendapatkan nilai pada setiap faktor hingar menggunakan sintaks `job_zne.result()[0].data.evs_noise_factors`. Seperti sebelum ini, kita boleh menggunakan keputusan ini secara naif untuk mendapatkan penyuaian linear dan mengekstrapolasi kepada kes hingar sifar, tetapi estimator dengan `resilience_level = 2` telah melakukan kerja yang lebih baik, dengan mengambil kira varians dan pertimbangan lain. Di bawah kita tunjukkan apa yang akan dihasilkan oleh ekstrapolasi linear, dan kita tunjukkan apa yang sebenarnya dihasilkan oleh ZNE terbina dalam.\n"

