msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d54a12ec-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that the built-in ZNE improved our estimate by over 15%, and worked quite a bit better than our attempt by hand.\n"
msgstr "Kita melihat bahawa ZNE terbina dalam memperbaiki anggaran kita lebih daripada 15%, dan berfungsi jauh lebih baik daripada percubaan manual kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving on, note that throughout this ZNE exploration, we have set `optimization_level = 1` in the pass manager. Higher levels of optimization reduce error, and sometimes the error reduction can make the errors scale less predictably. As is often the case, there is a balance: reduce errors, except when you are intentionally increasing them by a known factor.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum meneruskan, perhatikan bahawa sepanjang penerokaan ZNE ini, kita telah menetapkan `optimization_level = 1` dalam pass manager. Tahap pengoptimuman yang lebih tinggi mengurangkan ralat, dan kadangkala pengurangan ralat itu boleh menjadikan ralat berskala kurang boleh diramal. Seperti selalu, terdapat keseimbangan: kurangkan ralat, kecuali apabila anda sengaja meningkatkannya dengan faktor yang diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining methods {#combining-methods}"
msgstr "Menggabungkan kaedah {#combining-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE relies on the following:\n"
msgstr "ZNE bergantung pada perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A well-defined noise-scaling parameter $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Parameter penskalaan hingar $\\lambda$ yang tertakrif dengan baik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sufficiently smooth and predictable scaling of expectation values with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan nilai jangkaan dengan $\\lambda$ yang cukup lancar dan boleh diramal\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same effective noise channel, at different strengths\n"
msgstr "Saluran hingar berkesan yang sama, pada kekuatan yang berbeza\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "No bias introduced that does not scale with $\\lambda$\n"
msgstr "Tiada bias diperkenalkan yang tidak berskala dengan $\\lambda$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE combines cleanly with techniques that remove non-scaling biases (like M3) or make noise more regular (like twirling), but conflicts with techniques that either attempt to cancel noise entirely (PEC) or reshape it dynamically (DD).\n"
msgstr "ZNE boleh digabungkan dengan baik dengan teknik yang menghapuskan bias tidak berskala (seperti M3) atau menjadikan hingar lebih sekata (seperti twirling), tetapi bercanggah dengan teknik yang cuba membatalkan hingar sepenuhnya (PEC) atau membentuk semula hingar secara dinamik (DD).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, M3 addresses only measurement/readout error, which in practice can be treated as separate from gate errors (which are the focus of error scaling processes in ZNE). M3 is largely independent of gate folding; it can be cleanly combined with ZNE. TREX is very similar, and it can be combined with ZNE.\n"
msgstr "Khususnya, M3 hanya menangani ralat pengukuran/bacaan, yang dalam praktik boleh dianggap berasingan daripada ralat get (yang menjadi tumpuan proses penskalaan ralat dalam ZNE). M3 sebahagian besarnya bebas daripada gate folding; ia boleh digabungkan dengan bersih bersama ZNE. TREX sangat serupa, dan ia boleh digabungkan dengan ZNE.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling does focus on gates, unlike M3 and TREX. However, recall that Pauli twirling does not directly mitigate error/noise; rather, it changes it to make it more predictable. Pauli twirling might actually be beneficial to the ZNE process in making gate errors scale more linearly and thus make the extrapolation more accurate.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling memang menumpukan pada get, tidak seperti M3 dan TREX. Namun, ingat bahawa Pauli twirling tidak memitigasi ralat/hingar secara langsung; sebaliknya, ia mengubahnya supaya lebih boleh diramal. Pauli twirling mungkin sebenarnya bermanfaat kepada proses ZNE dengan menjadikan ralat get berskala lebih linear dan seterusnya menjadikan ekstrapolasi lebih tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dynamical decoupling (DD) is more nuanced. DD dynamically alters noise behavior by partially cancelling certain errors through the addition of gate sequences. If it is possible to construct circuits in such a way that DD behaves the same even when gates or blocks are folded, then in principle one could combine ZNE and DD, but in practice DD sometimes interferes with the scaling. If you want to combine them, things to consider include the following:\n"
"* Is DD applied consistently at all noise levels?\n"
"* Does folding preserve the DD structure?\n"
"* Does the resulting noise scaling still behave monotonically?\n"
msgstr ""
"Dynamical decoupling (DD) lebih bernuansa. DD mengubah tingkah laku hingar secara dinamik dengan membatalkan sebahagian ralat tertentu melalui penambahan jujukan get. Jika mungkin untuk membina litar sedemikian rupa sehingga DD berkelakuan sama walaupun apabila get atau blok dilipat, maka pada prinsipnya seseorang boleh menggabungkan ZNE dan DD, tetapi dalam praktik DD kadangkala mengganggu penskalaan. Jika anda ingin menggabungkannya, perkara yang perlu dipertimbangkan termasuk yang berikut:\n"
"* Adakah DD digunakan secara konsisten pada semua tahap hingar?\n"
"* Adakah pelipatan mengekalkan struktur DD?\n"
"* Adakah penskalaan hingar yang terhasil masih berkelakuan secara monotonik?\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last error mitigation method we will discuss as a standalone approach is not compatible with ZNE: probabilistic error cancellation.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah pengurangan ralat terakhir yang akan kita bincangkan sebagai pendekatan kendiri tidak serasi dengan ZNE: pembatalan ralat kebarangkalian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"
msgstr "Pembatalan Ralat Kebarangkalian (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike ZNE or measurement mitigation, PEC attempts to cancel noise at the gate level by reconstructing the ideal channel in expectation. Probabilistic Error Cancellation (PEC) is the most powerful and most expensive error-mitigation technique covered in this lesson. PEC is built around explicit inversion of the noise channel, carried out statistically rather than physically. PEC works by:\n"
msgstr "Tidak seperti ZNE atau pengurangan pengukuran, PEC cuba membatalkan hingar pada peringkat gate dengan membina semula saluran unggul dalam jangkaan. Pembatalan Ralat Kebarangkalian (PEC) ialah teknik pengurangan ralat yang paling berkuasa dan paling mahal yang diliputi dalam pelajaran ini. PEC dibina berdasarkan penyongsangan eksplisit saluran hingar, yang dijalankan secara statistik dan bukannya secara fizikal. PEC berfungsi dengan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise model in terms of a basis of \"error operations.\"\n"
msgstr "Mencirikan model hingar dari segi asas \"operasi ralat.\"\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressing the inverse of the noise channel as a quasi-probability distribution over physical operations.\n"
msgstr "Menyatakan songsangan saluran hingar sebagai taburan kuasi-kebarangkalian ke atas operasi fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling from this distribution during circuit execution to statistically construct an unbiased estimate of the ideal computation.\n"
msgstr "Membuat persampelan daripada taburan ini semasa pelaksanaan litar untuk membina secara statistik anggaran tidak berbias bagi pengiraan unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptually, PEC is like virtual error correction &mdash; it \"undoes\" noise by combining noisy operations in carefully weighted random patterns. Procedurally, however, PEC is not closely related to error correction or detection code. PEC's unbiased estimation of the ideal, noiseless expectation value comes at the cost of a very large sampling overhead and a strong dependence on accurate noise characterization.\n"
msgstr "Secara konsep, PEC adalah seperti pembetulan ralat maya &mdash; ia \"membuat asal\" hingar dengan menggabungkan operasi berhingar dalam corak rawak yang berpemberat dengan teliti. Namun, dari segi prosedur, PEC tidak berkait rapat dengan kod pembetulan atau pengesanan ralat. Anggaran tidak berbias PEC bagi nilai jangkaan unggul tanpa hingar datang dengan kos overhed persampelan yang sangat besar dan pergantungan yang kuat pada pencirian hingar yang tepat.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On IBM quantum computers, PEC is best viewed as a precision tool rather than a general-purpose mitigation layer: it is most appropriate for small circuits or small portions of larger circuits, benchmarking tasks, and high-accuracy studies where high quantum overhead is acceptable.\n"
msgstr "Pada komputer kuantum IBM, PEC paling baik dilihat sebagai alat ketepatan dan bukannya lapisan pengurangan serba guna: ia paling sesuai untuk litar kecil atau bahagian kecil litar yang lebih besar, tugas penanda aras, dan kajian ketepatan tinggi di mana overhed kuantum yang tinggi boleh diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characterizing the noise channel {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Mencirikan saluran hingar {#characterizing-the-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In PEC, each ideal gate in a quantum circuit is modeled as an **ideal unitary channel** followed by a noise process. Let $\\rho$ denote the density matrix of the quantum state. The ideal gate is represented by a unitary matrix $U$, which induces a quantum channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam PEC, setiap get unggul dalam litar kuantum dimodelkan sebagai **saluran uniter unggul** diikuti oleh proses hingar. Biarkan $\\rho$ melambangkan matriks ketumpatan keadaan kuantum. Get unggul diwakili oleh matriks uniter $U$, yang mendorong saluran kuantum:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}(\\rho) = U\\,\\rho\\,U^\\dagger.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On real hardware, this ideal evolution is corrupted by noise. We model the physical implementation of the gate as an **effective noisy channel**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\mathcal{N}$ is a noise channel capturing the stochastic errors associated with the gate. Throughout this discussion, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, and $\\mathcal{E}$ are linear maps acting on density operators. The ideal channel $\\mathcal{U}$ is unitary and reversible, while the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ (and hence $\\mathcal{E}$) is a completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP) map.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada perkakasan sebenar, evolusi unggul ini dicemari oleh hingar. Kita memodelkan pelaksanaan fizikal gate sebagai **saluran berhingar berkesan**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(\\mathcal{U}(\\rho)\\right)\n"
"= \\mathcal{N}\\!\\left(U\\rho U^\\dagger\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
"di mana $\\mathcal{N}$ ialah saluran hingar yang menangkap ralat stokastik yang berkaitan dengan gate. Sepanjang perbincangan ini, $\\mathcal{U}$, $\\mathcal{N}$, dan $\\mathcal{E}$ ialah pemetaan linear yang bertindak pada operator ketumpatan. Saluran unggul $\\mathcal{U}$ adalah uniter dan boleh balik, manakala saluran hingar $\\mathcal{N}$ (dan seterusnya $\\mathcal{E}$) ialah pemetaan positif sepenuhnya yang memelihara surih (CPTP).\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC assumes that the noise channel $\\mathcal{N}$ is known or approximately known. On IBM Quantum hardware, this information is typically obtained from device calibration data, error rates inferred from benchmarking experiments, and simplified noise models such as Pauli or depolarizing approximations for small gate sets. While PEC does not require a perfectly accurate noise model, its performance degrades rapidly as the assumed noise channel diverges from the true hardware behavior.\n"
msgstr "PEC mengandaikan bahawa saluran hingar $\\mathcal{N}$ diketahui atau diketahui secara hampir. Pada perkakasan IBM Quantum, maklumat ini lazimnya diperoleh daripada data penentukuran peranti, kadar ralat yang disimpulkan daripada eksperimen penanda aras, dan model hingar dipermudah seperti penghampiran Pauli atau depolarisasi bagi set gate yang kecil. Walaupun PEC tidak memerlukan model hingar yang tepat sepenuhnya, prestasinya merosot dengan pantas apabila saluran hingar yang diandaikan menyimpang daripada tingkah laku perkakasan sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decomposition of the inverse noise channel {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"
msgstr "Penguraian kuasi-kebarangkalian bagi saluran hingar songsang {#quasi-probability-decomposition-of-the-inverse-noise-channel}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The central idea of PEC is to **cancel the effect of noise in expectation** by constructing a stochastic approximation to the inverse of the noise channel. Formally, the goal is to apply a linear map that approximately undoes $\\mathcal{N}$, such that:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"in expectation over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Idea utama PEC ialah **membatalkan kesan hingar dalam jangkaan** dengan membina penghampiran stokastik bagi songsangan saluran hingar. Secara formal, matlamatnya ialah menggunakan pemetaan linear yang hampir membuat asal $\\mathcal{N}$, supaya:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} \\circ \\mathcal{E} \\;\\approx\\; \\mathcal{U}\n"
"$$\n"
"dalam jangkaan ke atas banyak pelaksanaan litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The inverse $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ is defined here as the algebraic inverse of $\\mathcal{N}$ treated as a linear superoperator acting on operators. This inverse exists only if $\\mathcal{N}$ is full-rank; non-invertible noise processes cannot be exactly mitigated using PEC.\n"
msgstr "Songsangan $\\mathcal{N}^{-1}$ ditakrifkan di sini sebagai songsangan algebra bagi $\\mathcal{N}$ yang dianggap sebagai superoperator linear yang bertindak pada operator. Songsangan ini wujud hanya jika $\\mathcal{N}$ berpangkat penuh; proses hingar tidak boleh songsang tidak boleh dimitigasi dengan tepat menggunakan PEC.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When inversion is possible, PEC expresses the inverse noise channel as a **linear combination of physically implementable operations**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Here, each $\\mathcal{O}_i$ is a noisy operation that can be executed on the hardware (typically native gates or short gate sequences), and the real coefficients $\\eta_i$ form a **quasi-probability distribution**. Unlike ordinary probabilities, the coefficients $\\eta_i$ might be negative or exceed 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila penyongsangan mungkin, PEC menyatakan saluran hingar songsang sebagai **gabungan linear operasi yang boleh dilaksanakan secara fizikal**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{N}^{-1} = \\sum_i \\eta_i\\, \\mathcal{O}_i.\n"
"$$\n"
"Di sini, setiap $\\mathcal{O}_i$ ialah operasi berhingar yang boleh dilaksanakan pada perkakasan (lazimnya gate natif atau jujukan gate pendek), dan pekali nyata $\\eta_i$ membentuk **taburan kuasi-kebarangkalian**. Tidak seperti kebarangkalian biasa, pekali $\\eta_i$ mungkin negatif atau melebihi 1.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **quasi-probability norm**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"quantifies the cost of the noise inversion. For any nontrivial noise channel, $\\gamma > 1$. On IBM Quantum hardware, this decomposition is typically performed:\n"
"- per gate or per small gate set,\n"
"- assuming restricted noise models (often Pauli-diagonal approximations),\n"
"- using backend-specific native operations and scheduling constraints.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Norma kuasi-kebarangkalian**:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma \\equiv \\sum_i |\\eta_i|\n"
"$$\n"
"mengukur kos penyongsangan hingar. Bagi mana-mana saluran hingar yang tidak remeh, $\\gamma > 1$. Pada perkakasan IBM Quantum, penguraian ini lazimnya dilakukan:\n"
"- bagi setiap gate atau setiap set gate kecil,\n"
"- dengan mengandaikan model hingar terhad (sering penghampiran pepenjuru Pauli),\n"
"- menggunakan operasi natif khusus Backend dan kekangan penjadualan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Monte Carlo reconstruction of the ideal circuit {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"
msgstr "Pembinaan semula Monte Carlo bagi litar unggul {#monte-carlo-reconstruction-of-the-ideal-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To estimate the expectation value of an observable $O$, PEC uses Monte Carlo sampling based on the decomposition above. For each occurrence of a noisy gate in the circuit, the following procedure is applied:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menganggarkan nilai jangkaan bagi observabel $O$, PEC menggunakan persampelan Monte Carlo berdasarkan penguraian di atas. Bagi setiap kemunculan get berhingar dalam litar, prosedur berikut digunakan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Randomly select an operation $\\mathcal{O}_i$ with probability:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih secara rawak satu operasi $\\mathcal{O}_i$ dengan kebarangkalian:\n"
"$$\n"
"p_i = \\frac{|\\eta_i|}{\\gamma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assign a classical weight:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tetapkan pemberat klasik:\n"
"$$\n"
"w_i = \\mathrm{sign}(\\eta_i).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the resulting randomized noisy circuit on the quantum backend.\n"
msgstr "Laksanakan litar berhingar rawak yang terhasil pada Backend kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiply the measured outcome by the product of all accumulated weights.\n"
msgstr "Darabkan hasil yang diukur dengan hasil darab semua pemberat terkumpul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Average the weighted results over many circuit executions.\n"
msgstr "Purata keputusan berpemberat ke atas banyak pelaksanaan litar.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The resulting estimator $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ satisfies\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"provided the noise model $\\mathcal{N}$ accurately describes the hardware. PEC therefore introduces **no systematic bias** in expectation, but replaces bias with **large statistical variance**. Each run produces a noisy but weighted estimate; only after averaging many such runs does the ideal expectation value emerge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penganggar yang terhasil $\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}$ memenuhi\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right] = \\langle O \\rangle_{\\mathrm{ideal}},\n"
"$$\n"
"selagi model hingar $\\mathcal{N}$ menerangkan perkakasan dengan tepat. Oleh itu PEC memperkenalkan **tiada pincang sistematik** dalam jangkaan, tetapi menggantikan pincang dengan **varians statistik yang besar**. Setiap larian menghasilkan anggaran berhingar tetapi berpemberat; hanya selepas mengambil purata banyak larian sedemikian barulah nilai jangkaan unggul muncul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual interpretation {#conceptual-interpretation}"
msgstr "Tafsiran konseptual {#conceptual-interpretation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is sometimes described as *virtual error correction*. While this phrasing is not entirely incorrect, it should not be confused with true quantum error correction. PEC involves no logical encoding, no syndrome extraction, and no real-time feedback. Errors are not prevented or corrected during circuit execution.\n"
msgstr "PEC kadangkala digambarkan sebagai *pembetulan ralat maya*. Walaupun frasa ini tidak sepenuhnya salah, ia tidak boleh dikelirukan dengan pembetulan ralat kuantum sebenar. PEC tidak melibatkan pengekodan logik, tiada pengekstrakan sindrom, dan tiada maklum balas masa nyata. Ralat tidak dicegah atau dibetulkan semasa pelaksanaan litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead, PEC cancels noise **statistically**, by combining many noisy circuit realizations with signed classical weights so that errors cancel only after classical post-processing. Information is not protected during execution; ideal results are reconstructed after the fact.\n"
msgstr "Sebaliknya, PEC membatalkan hingar **secara statistik**, dengan menggabungkan banyak realisasi litar berhingar dengan pemberat klasik bertanda supaya ralat hanya dibatalkan selepas pascapemprosesan klasik. Maklumat tidak dilindungi semasa pelaksanaan; keputusan unggul dibina semula selepas kejadian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resource scaling and cost {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"
msgstr "Penskalaan sumber dan kos {#resource-scaling-and-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dominant cost of PEC stems from variance amplification. The variance of the PEC estimator scales as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"implying:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Required number of shots} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kos dominan PEC berpunca daripada penguatan varians. Varians penganggar PEC berskala sebagai:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Var}\\!\\left(\\hat{O}_{\\mathrm{PEC}}\\right) \\propto \\gamma^2,\n"
"$$\n"
"yang membayangkan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\boxed{\\text{Bilangan shot yang diperlukan} \\;\\propto\\; \\gamma^2.}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This scaling is fundamental and cannot be improved through classical post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan ini adalah asas dan tidak dapat diperbaiki melalui pascapemprosesan klasik.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For circuits containing many noisy gates, each gate contributes a factor $\\gamma_k > 1$, causing the total quasi-probability norm to grow approximately multiplicatively:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $d$ is the circuit depth. On IBM Quantum hardware, this typically leads to exponential growth in sampling cost with circuit depth, with particularly strong sensitivity to two-qubit gate errors. This scaling places practical limits on the applicability of PEC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagi litar yang mengandungi banyak gate berhingar, setiap gate menyumbang faktor $\\gamma_k > 1$, menyebabkan jumlah norma kuasi-kebarangkalian meningkat kira-kira secara berganda:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\gamma_{\\mathrm{total}} \\sim \\prod_{k=1}^{d} \\gamma_k,\n"
"$$\n"
"di mana $d$ ialah kedalaman litar. Pada perkakasan IBM Quantum, ini lazimnya membawa kepada pertumbuhan eksponen dalam kos persampelan dengan kedalaman litar, dengan kepekaan yang amat kuat terhadap ralat gate dua qubit. Penskalaan ini meletakkan had praktikal pada kebolehgunaan PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is currently practical only when one or all of the following conditions are met:\n"
msgstr "PEC pada masa ini hanya praktikal apabila satu atau semua keadaan berikut dipenuhi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuits are very small or shallow (often $\\leq 10-20$ gates),\n"
msgstr "Litar sangat kecil atau cetek (selalunya $\\leq 10-20$ get),\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise models are simple and well-validated (for example, Pauli noise),\n"
msgstr "Model hingar mudah dan telah disahkan dengan baik (contohnya, hingar Pauli),\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High statistical cost is acceptable,\n"
msgstr "Kos statistik yang tinggi boleh diterima,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The goal is accuracy rather than throughput.\n"
msgstr "Matlamatnya ialah ketepatan dan bukannya daya pemprosesan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this reason, PEC is often applied to:\n"
msgstr "Atas sebab ini, PEC sering digunakan pada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Isolated subcircuits within larger workflows,\n"
msgstr "Sublitar terpencil dalam aliran kerja yang lebih besar,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short-time evolution steps,\n"
msgstr "Langkah evolusi masa singkat,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "State preparation or measurement routines,\n"
msgstr "Rutin penyediaan keadaan atau pengukuran,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarking and validation experiments.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen penanda aras dan pengesahan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IBM software stack (IBM Quantum Compute and error-mitigation tooling) reflects this by treating PEC as a specialized option, not a default mitigation layer.\n"
msgstr "Timbunan perisian IBM (IBM Quantum Compute dan alatan pengurangan ralat) mencerminkan hal ini dengan menganggap PEC sebagai pilihan khusus, bukan lapisan pengurangan lalai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical PEC use cases include:\n"
msgstr "Kes penggunaan PEC yang lazim termasuk:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Precision benchmarking of quantum hardware,\n"
msgstr "Penanda aras ketepatan perkakasan kuantum,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification of small quantum algorithms,\n"
msgstr "Pengesahan algoritma kuantum kecil,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-accuracy quantum chemistry on reduced systems,\n"
msgstr "Kimia kuantum berketepatan tinggi pada sistem yang dikurangkan,\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-checking ZNE or other mitigation methods.\n"
msgstr "Semakan silang ZNE atau kaedah pengurangan lain.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC's relationship to other mitigation methods {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"
msgstr "Hubungan PEC dengan kaedah pengurangan lain {#pecs-relationship-to-other-mitigation-methods}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many other mitigation techniques trade accuracy for scalability; PEC does just the opposite, focusing on accuracy above all else.\n"
msgstr "Banyak teknik pengurangan lain mengorbankan ketepatan demi kebolehskalaan; PEC melakukan sebaliknya, menumpukan pada ketepatan melebihi segala-galanya.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because PEC might only be used on a subcircuit, it is especially important here to ask what other mitigation methods can be combined with it. To reason clearly about compatibility with PEC, it helps to categorize techniques by what they do to the noise. Consider these general categories:\n"
msgstr "Oleh sebab PEC mungkin hanya digunakan pada sublitar, adalah amat penting di sini untuk bertanya kaedah pengurangan lain yang boleh digabungkan dengannya. Untuk membuat penaakulan yang jelas tentang keserasian dengan PEC, adalah berguna untuk mengkategorikan teknik mengikut kesannya terhadap hingar. Pertimbangkan kategori umum berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise cancellation - attempt to invert error channels\n"
msgstr "Pembatalan hingar - cuba menyongsangkan saluran ralat\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise scaling - deliberately increase noise to extrapolate\n"
msgstr "Penskalaan hingar - sengaja meningkatkan hingar untuk membuat ekstrapolasi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise reshaping - change the structure or spectrum of noise\n"
msgstr "Pembentukan semula hingar - mengubah struktur atau spektrum hingar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bias removal - correct errors that do not scale with gate noise\n"
msgstr "Penyingkiran pincang - membetulkan ralat yang tidak berskala dengan hingar gate\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC sits squarely in category (1). Any method that changes or rescales the noise channel must be examined carefully.\n"
msgstr "PEC terletak tepat dalam kategori (1). Mana-mana kaedah yang mengubah atau menskalakan semula saluran hingar mesti diteliti dengan berhati-hati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary table (high-level)\n"
msgstr "Jadual ringkasan (peringkat tinggi)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Technique | Compatible with PEC | Notes |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | No | Undoing versus scaling and sometimes tailoring error |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Yes (with care) | Affects error behavior, but might make it easier to learn |\n"
"| TREX | Yes | No overlap in workflow. Fully compatible. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Usually no | Changes error channel |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Teknik | Serasi dengan PEC | Catatan |\n"
"|-----------|---------------------|-------|\n"
"|    ZNE    | Tidak | Membatalkan berbanding menskalakan dan kadangkala menyesuaikan ralat |\n"
"|   Pauli twirling | Ya (dengan berhati-hati) | Menjejaskan tingkah laku ralat, tetapi mungkin menjadikannya lebih mudah dipelajari |\n"
"| TREX | Ya | Tiada pertindihan dalam aliran kerja. Sepenuhnya serasi. |\n"
"|Dynamical decoupling | Biasanya tidak | Mengubah saluran ralat |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and ZNE address the same error sources (gate errors) via mutually incompatible assumptions or workstreams, or both. For example, in ZNE, we assume error can be expanded in a parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"and that the error can be effectively scaled to model this expansion. PEC would undo the very error we rely on for the scaling. The parameter $\\lambda$ would become meaningless. Another way of thinking about it is:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC dan ZNE menangani sumber ralat yang sama (ralat gate) melalui andaian atau aliran kerja yang saling tidak serasi, atau kedua-duanya. Sebagai contoh, dalam ZNE, kita menganggap ralat boleh dikembangkan dalam parameter $\\lambda$:\n"
"$$\n"
"E(\\lambda) = E(0) + c_1 \\lambda + c_2 \\lambda^2 + \\cdots\n"
"$$\n"
"dan ralat itu boleh diskalakan dengan berkesan untuk memodelkan pengembangan ini. PEC akan membatalkan ralat yang menjadi asas penskalaan itu. Parameter $\\lambda$ akan menjadi tidak bermakna. Cara lain untuk memikirkannya ialah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying ZNE before PEC changes the noise channel you are trying to invert.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan ZNE sebelum PEC mengubah saluran hingar yang cuba anda songsangkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC before ZNE removes the very noise ZNE relies on to extrapolate.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan PEC sebelum ZNE menyingkirkan hingar yang menjadi asas ekstrapolasi ZNE.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC and ZNE should be considered alternative error-mitigation paradigms, not composable layers. Comparing them side-by-side is instructive, while combining them is not.\n"
msgstr "PEC dan ZNE harus dianggap sebagai paradigma pengurangan ralat alternatif, bukan lapisan yang boleh digubah. Membandingkan keduanya secara bersebelahan adalah bermanfaat, manakala menggabungkannya tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and Pauli twirling are generally compatible and often beneficial.\n"
"Twirling might help PEC in that twirling converts coherent errors into stochastic Pauli errors. This simplifies the noise channel, making it easier to represent and invert. For PEC, this is extremely valuable, for the following reasons:\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC dan Pauli twirling pada amnya serasi dan sering bermanfaat.\n"
"Twirling mungkin membantu PEC kerana twirling menukar ralat koheren kepada ralat Pauli stokastik. Ini memudahkan saluran hingar, menjadikannya lebih mudah diwakili dan disongsangkan. Bagi PEC, ini amat bernilai, atas sebab-sebab berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quasi-probability decompositions are much simpler for Pauli channels\n"
msgstr "Penguraian kuasi-kebarangkalian jauh lebih mudah untuk saluran Pauli\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quasi-probability norm $\\gamma$ is often significantly smaller\n"
msgstr "Norma kuasi-kebarangkalian $\\gamma$ sering jauh lebih kecil\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sampling variance is reduced\n"
msgstr "Varians pensampelan dikurangkan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Many PEC demonstrations assume or build in Pauli-twirled noise.\n"
"It's important to clarify that Pauli twirling does not mitigate errors by itself; it reshapes noise into a form that probabilistic error cancellation can handle more efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Banyak demonstrasi PEC menganggap atau membina hingar yang telah di-Pauli-twirl.\n"
"Adalah penting untuk menjelaskan bahawa Pauli twirling tidak memitigasi ralat dengan sendirinya; ia membentuk semula hingar kepada bentuk yang boleh dikendalikan dengan lebih cekap oleh pembatalan ralat probabilistik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC can and should be combined with TREX. These approaches are fully compatible and play orthogonal roles. TREX operates only at measurement, removes readout bias via randomized twirls of the measurement channel, and does not affect gate noise or circuit dynamics. PEC operates on gate noise. Because measurement error is additive rather than compositional, it is independent of gate sequences. It is safe and often desirable to apply TREX alongside PEC.\n"
msgstr "PEC boleh dan harus digabungkan dengan TREX. Pendekatan ini sepenuhnya serasi dan memainkan peranan ortogon. TREX hanya beroperasi pada pengukuran, menyingkirkan pincang bacaan melalui twirl rawak saluran pengukuran, dan tidak menjejaskan hingar gate atau dinamik litar. PEC beroperasi pada hingar gate. Oleh sebab ralat pengukuran bersifat tambahan dan bukan kompositional, ia tidak bergantung pada jujukan gate. Adalah selamat dan sering diingini untuk menggunakan TREX bersama PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering of these methods is what you might expect:\n"
"1. Execute PEC-randomized circuit\n"
"2. Apply TREX to mitigate readout error\n"
"3. Apply PEC weighting and averaging\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunan kaedah ini adalah seperti yang anda jangkakan:\n"
"1. Laksanakan litar rawak-PEC\n"
"2. Gunakan TREX untuk memitigasi ralat bacaan\n"
"3. Gunakan pemberat dan purata PEC\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEC and DD are generally incompatible unless the noise characterization used for PEC is performed with DD active. PEC assumes that $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"is stationary, repeatable, and accurately characterizable. DD explicitly reshapes the noise channel in time by modulating system-environment interactions and introducing non-trivial pulse-timing effects. As a result, the effective noise with DD is not the same channel as without DD. This is made even more complex by the fact that the noise channel can depend sensitively on circuit scheduling. The end result is that noise inversion becomes ill-defined or invalid.\n"
msgstr ""
"PEC dan DD pada amnya tidak serasi melainkan pencirian hingar yang digunakan untuk PEC dilakukan dengan DD aktif. PEC menganggap bahawa $N\\text{hardware noise} = \\mathcal N$\n"
"adalah pegun, boleh diulang, dan boleh dicirikan dengan tepat. DD secara eksplisit membentuk semula saluran hingar dalam masa dengan memodulasi interaksi sistem-persekitaran dan memperkenalkan kesan pemasaan denyut yang tidak remeh. Akibatnya, hingar berkesan dengan DD bukan saluran yang sama seperti tanpa DD. Ini menjadi lebih kompleks lagi kerana saluran hingar boleh bergantung dengan sensitif pada penjadualan litar. Hasil akhirnya ialah penyongsangan hingar menjadi tidak tertakrif atau tidak sah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is theoretically possible to characterize noise with DD active and build a PEC model accordingly, but this is highly advanced and not currently a recommended workflow.\n"
msgstr "Secara teori, adalah mungkin untuk mencirikan hingar dengan DD aktif dan membina model PEC dengan sewajarnya, tetapi ini sangat lanjutan dan bukan aliran kerja yang disyorkan pada masa ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying PEC by hand {#applying-pec-by-hand}"
msgstr "Menggunakan PEC secara manual {#applying-pec-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is complex and it is not recommended that you implement it by hand. Still, we want to work through the math of a basic application on a single qubit to understand what steps the process entails. We choose a mixed but nontrivial state so that we can see numerical effects clearly.\n"
msgstr "PEC adalah kompleks dan tidak disyorkan anda melaksanakannya secara manual. Walaupun begitu, kita ingin menyelesaikan matematik bagi aplikasi asas pada satu qubit untuk memahami langkah yang terlibat dalam proses ini. Kita memilih keadaan campuran tetapi tidak remeh supaya kita dapat melihat kesan berangka dengan jelas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Take a qubit that should be in the pure state\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ambil satu qubit yang sepatutnya berada dalam keadaan tulen\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi \\rangle & = \\cos(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\tfrac{\\pi}{6})\\lvert 1\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\lvert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{2}\\lvert 1\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ideal density matrix is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks ketumpatan unggul ialah:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{ideal}} = \\lvert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\rvert\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"We've chosen this density matrix because it is not diagonal and is only for a single qubit so that it is tractable to examine \"by hand\".\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Kita memilih matriks ketumpatan ini kerana ia bukan pepenjuru dan hanya untuk satu qubit supaya mudah diperiksa \"secara manual\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now apply a very simple, but realistic noise model: a single-qubit depolarizing channel, with small strength $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini kita menggunakan model hingar yang sangat mudah, tetapi realistik: saluran depolarisasi satu qubit, dengan kekuatan kecil $p$.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = (1 - p)\\rho + \\frac{p}{3}\n"
"(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep the arithmetic friendly, take $p = 0.15$. This channel is completely positive, trace-preserving (CPTP), as it must be. It is a realistic noise channel for real hardware, or at least realistic for describing some of the noise. Further, this noise channel is analytically invertible, as a linear map. In other words, there exists an inverse matrix, but that doesn't mean that the matrix corresponds to a CPTP physical channel, and it certainly doesn't correspond to a unitary that could be implemented on hardware.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memudahkan aritmetik, ambil $p = 0.15$. Saluran ini positif sepenuhnya dan mengekalkan surih (CPTP), sebagaimana yang sepatutnya. Ia ialah saluran hingar yang realistik untuk perkakasan sebenar, atau sekurang-kurangnya realistik untuk menerangkan sebahagian hingar. Selanjutnya, saluran hingar ini boleh disongsangkan secara analitik, sebagai peta linear. Dalam erti kata lain, wujud matriks songsang, tetapi itu tidak bermakna matriks tersebut sepadan dengan saluran fizikal CPTP, dan ia pastinya tidak sepadan dengan uniter yang boleh dilaksanakan pada perkakasan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we apply our depolarizing noise channel to our single-qubit density matrix and obtain:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"With $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ and $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita menggunakan saluran hingar depolarisasi kita pada matriks ketumpatan satu qubit kita dan memperoleh:\n"
"$$\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = \\left(1 - \\frac{4p}{3}\\right)\\rho\n"
"+ \\frac{2p}{3} I.\n"
"$$\n"
"Dengan $p = 0.15$: $\\frac{4p}{3} = 0.20$ dan $\\frac{2p}{3} = 0.10$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"So:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}(\\rho) = 0.8 \\rho + 0.1 I.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying this to our state:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan ini pada keadaan kita:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.8\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"0.1\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute explicitly:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung secara eksplisit:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{noisy}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"This is still a physical density matrix, and it still has trace one &mdash; but it is more mixed now.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad \\text{(rounded)}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Ini masih matriks ketumpatan fizikal, dan ia masih mempunyai surih satu &mdash; tetapi kini ia lebih bercampur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we compute the ideal inverse channel, but being very prepared for the possibility that it might not be physical. We will check whether it is. Mathematically, the inverse linear map is:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita mengira saluran songsang unggul, tetapi bersedia sepenuhnya untuk kemungkinan bahawa ia mungkin tidak fizikal. Kita akan menyemak sama ada ia fizikal. Secara matematik, peta linear songsang ialah:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"\\rho - 0.1 I\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If this inverse action were itself a valid physical channel, then we would be tempted to try to implement it exactly. Of course, we would still need to figure out how to implement it using unitary operations and classical steps, but implementing this would be the goal. However, it turns out this is *not* CPTP, and there is generally no guarantee that such inverse mappings will be CPTP. That is critical to our current discussion, because it is the reason PEC exists.\n"
msgstr "Jika tindakan songsang ini sendiri ialah saluran fizikal yang sah, maka kita akan tergoda untuk cuba melaksanakannya dengan tepat. Sudah tentu, kita masih perlu mencari cara untuk melaksanakannya menggunakan operasi unitari dan langkah klasik, tetapi melaksanakannya akan menjadi matlamat. Walau bagaimanapun, ternyata ini *bukan* CPTP, dan pada amnya tiada jaminan bahawa pemetaan songsang sedemikian akan menjadi CPTP. Itu penting untuk perbincangan kita sekarang, kerana itulah sebab PEC wujud.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might be able to see that it is not CPTP just by looking at it. A sure-fire check is to apply it to a density matrix and see if it returns physical results. This is left as an exercise to check your understanding.\n"
msgstr "Anda mungkin dapat melihat bahawa ia bukan CPTP hanya dengan melihatnya. Semakan yang pasti ialah menggunakannya pada matriks ketumpatan dan melihat sama ada ia memberikan hasil yang fizikal. Ini ditinggalkan sebagai latihan untuk menyemak kefahaman anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether the inverse mapping from above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ is CPTP by applying it to a new density matrix:\n"
msgstr "Semak sama ada pemetaan songsang $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ di atas ialah CPTP dengan menggunakannya pada matriks ketumpatan baharu:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{test}}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.95 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.05\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results as being physical or non-physical.\n"
msgstr "Tafsirkan hasilnya sebagai fizikal atau bukan fizikal.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_{\\text{test}}) & = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\rho_{\\text{test}} - 0.1 I\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{0.8} \\left(\\begin{pmatrix} 0.95 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.05 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0.1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.1 \\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix} 1.0625 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -0.0625 \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a physical density matrix, this corresponds to a classical probability of greater than 1 that the system is in the state $|0\\rangle$ and a negative probability of being in the state $|1\\rangle$. Clearly this mapping can yield nonsense density matrices. Further, by inspection we can see that the eigenvalues of the resulting density matrix are 1.0625 and -0.0625, meaning not all eigenvalues are positive. Thus the mapping is not \"completely positive\", the \"CP\" in CPTP.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai matriks ketumpatan fizikal, ini sepadan dengan kebarangkalian klasik lebih besar daripada 1 bahawa sistem berada dalam keadaan $|0\\rangle$ dan kebarangkalian negatif untuk berada dalam keadaan $|1\\rangle$. Jelas sekali pemetaan ini boleh menghasilkan matriks ketumpatan yang tidak masuk akal. Selanjutnya, melalui pemeriksaan kita dapat melihat bahawa nilai eigen bagi matriks ketumpatan yang terhasil ialah 1.0625 dan -0.0625, bermakna bukan semua nilai eigen adalah positif. Oleh itu pemetaan ini bukan \"positif sepenuhnya\", iaitu \"CP\" dalam CPTP.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check by explicit calculation that the inverse operation above $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ undoes the noise channel and returns the noise-free state.\n"
msgstr "Semak melalui pengiraan eksplisit bahawa operasi songsang $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ di atas membatalkan saluran hingar dan mengembalikan keadaan tanpa hingar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply it to the noisy state:\n"
msgstr "Gunakannya pada keadaan berhingar:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\text{recovered}} & = \\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho_\\text{noisy})\\\\\n"
" & =\\frac{1}{0.8} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"-\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"This is exactly the original state (up to rounding).\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0.1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\frac{1}{0.8}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.6 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.2\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
"& \\approx\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.75 & 0.433 \\\\\n"
"0.433 & 0.25\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Ini betul-betul keadaan asal (sehingga pembundaran).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We restate to be absolutely clear: we cannot invert the noise channel exactly; the inverse is not CPTP, nor is it a valid physical channel. However, we can effectively invert the channel as a linear combination of physical channels.\n"
msgstr "Kita nyatakan semula agar benar-benar jelas: kita tidak boleh menyongsangkan saluran hingar dengan tepat; songsangnya bukan CPTP, dan ia juga bukan saluran fizikal yang sah. Walau bagaimanapun, kita boleh menyongsangkan saluran itu dengan berkesan sebagai gabungan linear saluran fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the depolarizing channel:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"where: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk saluran depolarisasi:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I}\n"
"+ \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"dengan: $\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X$ dan seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The inverse can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Songsangnya boleh ditulis sebagai:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}=\\sum_j \\eta_j \\mathcal{P}_j\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with:\n"
msgstr "with:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = physically implementable Clifford channels\n"
msgstr "$\\mathcal{P}_j$ = saluran Clifford yang boleh dilaksanakan secara fizikal\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\eta_j$ = quasi-probabilities\n"
msgstr "$\\eta_j$ = kuasi-kebarangkalian\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"
msgstr "Some $\\eta_j < 0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the core idea behind PEC:\n"
msgstr "Ini ialah idea teras di sebalik PEC:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample channels according to $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"
msgstr "Sampel saluran mengikut $|\\eta_j|$∣\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Attach signs to measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Lampirkan tanda pada hasil pengukuran\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expectation values converge to the noise-free value\n"
msgstr "Nilai jangkaan menumpu kepada nilai tanpa hingar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We apply PEC \"by hand\" to the estimation of $\\langle Z \\rangle$ by using the density matrix $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ and see if we can recover the results for $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. For $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ we expect:\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan PEC \"secara manual\" pada penganggaran $\\langle Z \\rangle$ dengan menggunakan matriks ketumpatan $\\rho_\\text{noisy}$ dan melihat sama ada kita dapat memulihkan hasil untuk $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$. Untuk $\\rho_\\text{ideal}$ kita jangkakan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} & =\\text{Tr}(Z \\rho_\\text{ideal})\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n"
"-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\n"
"&=0.5\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that for the noisy density matrix, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan juga bahawa untuk matriks ketumpatan berhingar, kita memperoleh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{noisy} & =\\text{Tr}\\left(Z \\rho_\\text{noisy}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left( \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"0.346 & 0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = \\text{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.7 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.3\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\\\\\n"
"&=0.7-0.3\\\\\n"
"&=0.4\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's the right order of magnitude but significantly far from the ideal case.\n"
msgstr "Ia berada pada tertib magnitud yang betul tetapi jauh berbeza daripada kes unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we step through how, with the PEC process, we can reconstruct the unbiased expectation value from the noisy density matrix. In real workflows, this is probabilistic and will be automated. In this \"by-hand\" workflow, we will choose probabilistic values that are realistic, but perhaps convenient for our presentation. This should not be taken as a claim that PEC is perfect. This is simply to show you a plausible scenario that could happen inside the PEC packages.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita meneliti bagaimana, dengan proses PEC, kita boleh membina semula nilai jangkaan tidak pincang daripada matriks ketumpatan berhingar. Dalam aliran kerja sebenar, ini bersifat probabilistik dan akan diautomasikan. Dalam aliran kerja \"manual\" ini, kita akan memilih nilai probabilistik yang realistik, tetapi mungkin mudah untuk pembentangan kita. Ini tidak harus dianggap sebagai dakwaan bahawa PEC adalah sempurna. Ini hanyalah untuk menunjukkan kepada anda senario munasabah yang boleh berlaku di dalam pakej PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that our noise channel is of the form:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"The inverse can be written (exactly):\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahawa saluran hingar kita berbentuk:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E} = (1 - p)\\mathcal{I} + \\frac{p}{3}(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"Songsangnya boleh ditulis (dengan tepat):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
"based on symmetry of the transformation and the completeness of the Pauli operators. Inverting the noise channel somehow in the estimation process should yield an estimator that is unbiased and normalized. To do this, we must at least determine the coefficents $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ and then think about how to implement the inverse transformation. When done by a noise learner, the inversion of this noise channel would be done at the channel level, independent of a specific case like our density matrix. The coefficients $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ would come from this inversion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is simpler for this introduction to focus on the channel's effect on our density matrix. This allows us to work with familiar objects like density matrices and expectation values. To that end, consider what must be true about the effects of this inverse operation on our estimation process: the estimator produced by PEC must be normalized and unbiased. This corresponds to two conditions:\n"
msgstr "Untuk pengenalan ini, lebih mudah menumpukan pada kesan saluran terhadap matriks ketumpatan kita. Ini membolehkan kita bekerja dengan objek yang biasa seperti matriks ketumpatan dan nilai jangkaan. Untuk tujuan itu, pertimbangkan apa yang mesti benar tentang kesan operasi songsang ini terhadap proses penganggaran kita: penganggar yang dihasilkan oleh PEC mestilah ternormal dan tidak pincang. Ini sepadan dengan dua syarat:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization: To ensure that this operation does not change the scale of the observable, we require that $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. To see why this is the case, we could either consider the action of the inverse on a density matrix, or consider its action on the expectation value of something trivial like $\\mathcal{I}$ itself.\n"
msgstr "Normalisasi: Untuk memastikan operasi ini tidak mengubah skala observable, kita memerlukan $\\alpha+3\\beta = 1$. Untuk melihat mengapa begitu, kita boleh mempertimbangkan tindakan songsang pada matriks ketumpatan, atau mempertimbangkan tindakannya pada nilai jangkaan sesuatu yang remeh seperti $\\mathcal{I}$ itu sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calibration: In a real workflow, we use calibration circuits to learn noise behavior at a gate level. We then use the gate-level knowledge of noise behavior, and the linearity of expectation values to apply the learned noise model to the larger circuit. In our case, we started with artificial knowledge that the ideal expectation value $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. But it would be very easy to come up with a state for which we know theoretically that this would be the ideal value, and then use actual measurements for calibration. A key point is that for PEC, one typically does not learn a full noise model of the entire circuit. Instead, one learns local noise models for individual gates or circuit layers and uses those to construct the quasi-probability decomposition.\n"
msgstr "Penentukuran: Dalam aliran kerja sebenar, kita menggunakan litar penentukuran untuk mempelajari tingkah laku hingar pada peringkat gate. Kita kemudian menggunakan pengetahuan peringkat gate tentang tingkah laku hingar, dan kelinearan nilai jangkaan untuk menggunakan model hingar yang dipelajari pada litar yang lebih besar. Dalam kes kita, kita bermula dengan pengetahuan buatan bahawa nilai jangkaan unggul ialah $\\langle Z \\rangle = 0.5$. Tetapi adalah sangat mudah untuk mencipta keadaan yang secara teori kita tahu bahawa ini ialah nilai unggul, dan kemudian menggunakan pengukuran sebenar untuk penentukuran. Satu perkara utama ialah bagi PEC, biasanya seseorang tidak mempelajari model hingar penuh bagi keseluruhan litar. Sebaliknya, seseorang mempelajari model hingar tempatan untuk gate atau lapisan litar individu dan menggunakannya untuk membina penguraian kuasi-kebarangkalian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We use these conditions to determine $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. We consider the ansatz\n"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan syarat-syarat ini untuk menentukan $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$. Kita pertimbangkan ansatz\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\mathcal{I} + \\beta(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z}),\n"
"$$\n"
"and apply it to an arbitrary single-qubit density matrix $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the Pauli channels act by conjugation:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahawa saluran Pauli bertindak melalui konjugasi:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{X}(\\rho) = X\\rho X, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Y}(\\rho) = Y\\rho Y, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{Z}(\\rho) = Z\\rho Z.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ to $\\rho$ gives:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan $\\mathcal{E}^{-1}$ pada $\\rho$ memberikan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\alpha\\,\\rho\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\left(X\\rho X + Y\\rho Y + Z\\rho Z\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taking the trace, we obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengambil surih, kita memperoleh:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"&=\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta\\Big(\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(X\\rho X)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Y\\rho Y)\n"
"+\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(Z\\rho Z)\n"
"\\Big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Pauli operator is unitary, such that conjugation preserves the trace:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap pengendali Pauli ialah unitari, supaya konjugasi mengekalkan surih:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}(P\\rho P) = \\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho),\n"
"\\qquad P \\in \\{X,Y,Z\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Therefore,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"(\\alpha + 3\\beta)\\,\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the PEC estimator to be normalized, the effective\n"
"inverse map must preserve the trace of all density matrices. That is, we require:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"Agar penganggar PEC ternormal, peta songsang berkesan\n"
"mesti mengekalkan surih semua matriks ketumpatan. Iaitu, kita memerlukan:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{Tr}\\!\\left[\\mathcal{E}^{-1}(\\rho)\\right]\n"
"=\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\mathrm{Tr}(\\rho)\n"
"\\qquad \\text{for all } \\rho.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies the normalization constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini membayangkan kekangan normalisasi:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\alpha + 3\\beta = 1.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But in our case, this yields the condition:\n"
msgstr "Tetapi dalam kes kita, ini menghasilkan syarat:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"& =\n"
"\\alpha(+0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(-0.4)\n"
"+\n"
"\\beta(+0.4)\n"
"& = 0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we use calibration information to relate the observed expectation value to the known ideal one.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita menggunakan maklumat penentukuran untuk mengaitkan nilai jangkaan yang diperhatikan dengan nilai unggul yang diketahui.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{PEC}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"\\langle Z\\rangle_\\text{ideal}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Or equivalently,\n"
"$$\n"
"0.4(\\alpha-\\beta)=0.5\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving our two conditions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, we obtain:\n"
msgstr "Menyelesaikan dua syarat kita untuk $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$, kita memperoleh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\alpha = 1.1875\\\\\n"
"\\beta = -0.0625\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These coefficients sum to 1, but one of them is negative.\n"
msgstr "Pekali ini berjumlah 1, tetapi salah satunya negatif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can recover the ideal expectation value by randomly modifying the circuit, measuring, multiplying the result by a signed weight, and averaging. In particular, no density matrices are reconstructed and no inverse channel is implemented physically.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh memulihkan nilai jangkaan unggul dengan mengubah suai litar secara rawak, mengukur, mendarabkan hasilnya dengan pemberat bertanda, dan mengambil purata. Khususnya, tiada matriks ketumpatan dibina semula dan tiada saluran songsang dilaksanakan secara fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The key step: this is PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"
msgstr "Langkah utama: inilah PEC {#the-key-step-this-is-pec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For our noise strength $p=0.15$, the inverse channel can be written as:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{E}^{-1} =\\underbrace{1.1875}_{\\alpha}\\,\\mathcal{I}\n"
"\\;+\\;\n"
"\\underbrace{(-0.0625)}_{\\beta}\n"
"(\\mathcal{X} + \\mathcal{Y} + \\mathcal{Z})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
