"0.3 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.7\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\text{Tr}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.3 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.7\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\text{Tr}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.3 & 0.346 \\\\\n"
"-0.346 & -0.7\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = 0.3 - 0.7 = -0.4\n"
msgstr "& = 0.3 - 0.7 = -0.4\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Y and Z proceed exactly as above.\n"
msgstr "Y dan Z dikendalikan dengan cara yang sama seperti di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now rewrite our overall expectation value as:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita boleh menulis semula nilai jangkaan keseluruhan kita sebagai:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC} & = W \\sum_{i\\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}} p_i \\times \\text{sign}_i \\times \\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}\\\\\n"
"& = (1.375)\\times \\left((0.864)(+1)(0.40)+(0.045)(-1)(-0.40)+(0.045)(-1)(-0.40)+(0.045)(-1)(0.40)\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = (1.375)\\times(0.364)\\\\\n"
"& = (0.50)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{PEC} & = W \\sum_{i\\in \\{I, X, Y, Z\\}} p_i \\times \\text{sign}_i \\times \\langle Z \\rangle_{P_i}\\\\\n"
"& = (1.375)\\times \\left((0.864)(+1)(0.40)+(0.045)(-1)(-0.40)+(0.045)(-1)(-0.40)+(0.045)(-1)(0.40)\\right)\\\\\n"
"& = (1.375)\\times(0.364)\\\\\n"
"& = (0.50)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we know the parameters $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ for our gate noise (or more parameters for more complex noise channels), that is sufficient to determine (1) the overall weight factor, and (2) the probabilities with which we should apply the Pauli operators. What this result above shows is that if we do that, we mitigate the noise and recover unbiased expectation values. The average over all these shots converged to  $\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} = 0.5$, even though:\n"
msgstr "Jika kita mengetahui parameter $\\alpha$ dan $\\beta$ bagi hingar gate kita (atau lebih banyak parameter untuk saluran hingar yang lebih kompleks), itu sudah memadai untuk menentukan (1) faktor pemberat keseluruhan, dan (2) kebarangkalian untuk kita menggunakan pengendali Pauli. Apa yang ditunjukkan oleh keputusan di atas ialah jika kita melakukannya, kita mengurangkan hingar dan memulihkan nilai jangkaan yang tidak berat sebelah. Purata bagi semua shot ini menumpu kepada $\\langle Z \\rangle_\\text{ideal} = 0.5$, walaupun:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Individual shots give contributions that are larger than ±1\n"
msgstr "Shot individu memberikan sumbangan yang lebih besar daripada ±1\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some shots have negative statistical weight\n"
msgstr "Sesetengah shot mempunyai pemberat statistik yang negatif\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every quantum operation was physical\n"
msgstr "Setiap operasi kuantum adalah fizikal\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of PEC workflow {#overview-of-pec-workflow}"
msgstr "Gambaran keseluruhan aliran kerja PEC {#overview-of-pec-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In PEC, all steps on the quantum computer are:\n"
msgstr "Dalam PEC, semua langkah pada komputer kuantum ialah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise learning\n"
msgstr "Pembelajaran hingar\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "State preparation for your target circuit\n"
msgstr "Penyediaan keadaan untuk litar sasaran anda\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply Pauli gates probabilistically as described above\n"
msgstr "Gunakan gate Pauli secara kebarangkalian seperti yang diterangkan di atas\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurement\n"
msgstr "Measurement\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The effective inverse noise map is realized statistically in classical post-processing. This allows for more general inversion of noise channels that would otherwise have required non-physical steps like negative probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Peta hingar songsang yang berkesan direalisasikan secara statistik dalam pasca-pemprosesan klasik. Ini membolehkan penyongsangan saluran hingar yang lebih umum yang sebaliknya memerlukan langkah tidak fizikal seperti kebarangkalian negatif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The price we pay for this is variance.\n"
"Each shot formerly had a \"magnitude\" equal to the possible measurement outcome magnitudes $|\\pm 1| = 1$. After scaling by the weight factor $W$, it has magnitude $W$ (1.375 in our example above).\n"
"$$\n"
"\\text{variance} \\propto W^2 \\approx 1.89\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Harga yang kita bayar untuk ini ialah varians.\n"
"Setiap shot sebelum ini mempunyai \"magnitud\" yang sama dengan magnitud hasil pengukuran yang mungkin $|\\pm 1| = 1$. Selepas penskalaan dengan faktor pemberat $W$, magnitudnya menjadi $W$ (1.375 dalam contoh kita di atas).\n"
"$$\n"
"\\text{variance} \\propto W^2 \\approx 1.89\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the origin of the sampling overhead of PEC.\n"
msgstr "Itulah punca overhead pensampelan PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Built-in PEC {#built-in-pec}"
msgstr "PEC terbina dalam {#built-in-pec}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we will use PEC as it is built into IBM Quantum primitives. It is critical here to distinguish between full gate-level PEC and a local noise learning model for more scalable PEC, which is used by IBM Quantum primitives. The overhead of using full PEC would would restrict our application of it to small circuits. That's fine, but it is more useful to have a tool that can scale to a size at which quantum computing becomes valuable for real-world problems. For this reason, IBM Quantum primtives use a layer-wise PEC using a learned Pauli-Lindblad noise model, with aggressive scalability safeguards. In this implementation of PEC, noise is learned per repeated circuit layer, not per gate instance, and the noise model is Pauli-twirled, local, and Markovian. Clifford gates are absorbed into the noise model, while non-Clifford gates dominate the mitigation cost. Sampling overhead is capped to avoid exponential blow-ups.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita akan menggunakan PEC seperti yang terbina dalam primitif IBM Quantum. Di sini penting untuk membezakan antara PEC peringkat gate penuh dengan model pembelajaran hingar tempatan untuk PEC yang lebih berskala, yang digunakan oleh primitif IBM Quantum. Overhed menggunakan PEC penuh akan mengehadkan penggunaannya kepada litar kecil. Itu tidak mengapa, tetapi lebih berguna untuk mempunyai alat yang boleh diskalakan ke saiz di mana pengkomputeran kuantum menjadi bernilai untuk masalah dunia sebenar. Atas sebab ini, primitif IBM Quantum menggunakan PEC mengikut lapisan dengan model hingar Pauli-Lindblad yang dipelajari, dengan perlindungan kebolehskalaan yang agresif. Dalam pelaksanaan PEC ini, hingar dipelajari bagi setiap lapisan litar yang berulang, bukan bagi setiap contoh gate, dan model hingar tersebut ialah Pauli-twirled, tempatan dan Markovian. Gate Clifford diserap ke dalam model hingar, manakala gate bukan Clifford mendominasi kos pengurangan. Overhed pensampelan dihadkan untuk mengelakkan letusan eksponen.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will apply the PEC built in to IBM Quantum primitives at two scales: small (six qubits) and mid-sized (30 qubits) to see how cost is kept management in this version of PEC. Within each size experiment, we will also explicitly compare the results from PEC to those with no mitigation, with ZNE, and to the ideal value.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan PEC yang terbina dalam primitif IBM Quantum pada dua skala: kecil (enam qubit) dan bersaiz sederhana (30 qubit) untuk melihat bagaimana kos dikawal dalam versi PEC ini. Dalam setiap eksperimen saiz, kita juga akan membandingkan secara eksplisit keputusan PEC dengan keputusan tanpa pengurangan, dengan ZNE, dan dengan nilai unggul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start by importing a few necessary packages.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulakan dengan mengimport beberapa pakej yang diperlukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We choose an observable to estimate. The observable below is the Hamiltonian of a chain of Ising-like spins with nearest-neighbor coupling only in the $X$ component of their interaction, and a single-qubit term in $Z$, as though due to an external field in $Z$.\n"
msgstr "Kita memilih observable untuk dianggarkan. Observable di bawah ialah Hamiltonian bagi rantai spin seakan-Ising dengan gandingan jiran terdekat sahaja pada komponen $X$ interaksi mereka, dan satu sebutan qubit tunggal dalam $Z$, seolah-olah disebabkan oleh medan luar dalam $Z$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{H} = J_X\\sum_i{X_iX_{i+1}}+B\\sum_i{Z_i}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{H} = J_X\\sum_i{X_iX_{i+1}}+B\\sum_i{Z_i}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is no special reason for the selection of this Hamiltonian. We simply need a combination of an observable and circuit that is non-trivial so that error mitigation can do its work. We explicitly scale the Hamiltonian (using the coefficients), dividing out the number of qubits so that the energy will remain at the same order of magnitude as we increase the number of qubits. We begin with only six.\n"
msgstr "Tiada sebab istimewa untuk pemilihan Hamiltonian ini. Kita hanya memerlukan gabungan observable dan litar yang tidak remeh supaya pengurangan ralat dapat berfungsi. Kita menskala Hamiltonian secara eksplisit (menggunakan pekali), dengan membahagikan bilangan qubit supaya tenaga kekal pada susunan magnitud yang sama apabila kita menambah bilangan qubit. Kita bermula dengan hanya enam.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in the choice of Hamiltonian, the circuit for state preparation below is not chosen for any physical reasons. Rather, it is chosen to have sufficient two-qubit depth and sufficiently many non-Clifford gates that PEC can be useful. There is no reason to think that this circuit is a good approximation of the ground state of this chain of spins, for example.\n"
msgstr "Seperti dalam pemilihan Hamiltonian, litar untuk penyediaan keadaan di bawah tidak dipilih atas sebab fizikal. Sebaliknya, ia dipilih supaya mempunyai kedalaman dua-qubit yang mencukupi dan gate bukan Clifford yang cukup banyak supaya PEC boleh berguna. Tiada sebab untuk menganggap litar ini sebagai penghampiran yang baik bagi keadaan dasar rantai spin ini, sebagai contoh.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d61a4174-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d61a4174-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We transpile our circuit and apply the resulting layout to our observables.\n"
msgstr "Kita mentranspil litar kita dan menggunakan susun atur yang terhasil pada observable kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We obtain the ideal expectation value using the Statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "Kita memperoleh nilai jangkaan ideal menggunakan simulator Statevector.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We expect that other ideal values will be similar in size. Now we run this on a real IBM quantum computer with no error mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Kita menjangkakan nilai unggul yang lain akan mempunyai saiz yang serupa. Sekarang kita jalankan ini pada komputer kuantum IBM sebenar tanpa pengurangan ralat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we apply ZNE to the same problem.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita gunakan ZNE pada masalah yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we apply PEC.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kita gunakan PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below we plot our results and compare.\n"
msgstr "Di bawah kita plotkan keputusan kita dan membandingkannya.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/626e82d3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/626e82d3-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This worked very well. Our estimate using PEC is just 0.2% from the ideal value.\n"
msgstr "Ini berfungsi dengan sangat baik. Anggaran kita menggunakan PEC hanya 0.2% daripada nilai ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But remember how the quantum overhead grows exponentially. We enforced a maximum overhead of `max_overhead = 100`. From the time and the quality of the results, it looks like we might not have hit that maximum. However, if we scale up our calculation and leave that maximum in place, we will hit it, and our results will suffer.\n"
msgstr "Tetapi ingat bagaimana overhead kuantum meningkat secara eksponen. Kita menguatkuasakan overhead maksimum `max_overhead = 100`. Berdasarkan masa dan kualiti keputusan, nampaknya kita mungkin tidak mencapai maksimum itu. Walau bagaimanapun, jika kita menskalakan pengiraan kita dan mengekalkan maksimum itu, kita akan mencapainya, dan keputusan kita akan terjejas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can see what happens when we scale our circuit up to 30 qubits. Interestingly, on many laptops the Statevector simulator will start to time out around 24-28 qubits. We could find computational ways around this. But instead, let's embrace the fact that quantum computers will be able to solve some problems at a scale at which classical computers cannot keep up. That is the point. What can we do, then, to validate our quantum computing results in those cases? There are several potential answers:\n"
"* Some problems are difficult to solve but easy to check (like prime factoring as in Shor's algorithm).\n"
"* Some problems have parameter regimes or flavors of the problem that reduce in complexity and can be solved classically, or even analytically, to compare a few points.\n"
"In this case, we chose a Hamiltonian that is intrinsic (we divided out the number of qubits). The ideal expectation value should be fairly stable. Let's see how the ideal expectation value varies with the number of qubits and see if we can make classical predictions about the value at 30 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh melihat apa yang berlaku apabila kita menskalakan litar kita ke 30 qubit. Menariknya, pada kebanyakan komputer riba simulator Statevector akan mula tamat masa sekitar 24-28 qubit. Kita boleh mencari jalan pengiraan untuk mengatasinya. Tetapi sebaliknya, mari kita terima hakikat bahawa komputer kuantum akan dapat menyelesaikan sesetengah masalah pada skala yang tidak dapat diikuti oleh komputer klasik. Itulah intinya. Jadi, apakah yang boleh kita lakukan untuk mengesahkan keputusan pengkomputeran kuantum kita dalam kes sedemikian? Terdapat beberapa jawapan yang berpotensi:\n"
"* Sesetengah masalah sukar diselesaikan tetapi mudah disemak (seperti pemfaktoran perdana dalam algoritma Shor).\n"
"* Sesetengah masalah mempunyai rejim parameter atau variasi masalah yang kompleksitinya berkurang dan boleh diselesaikan secara klasik, atau malah secara analisis, untuk membandingkan beberapa titik.\n"
"Dalam kes ini, kita memilih Hamiltonian yang intrinsik (kita membahagikan bilangan qubit). Nilai jangkaan ideal sepatutnya agak stabil. Mari kita lihat bagaimana nilai jangkaan ideal berubah mengikut bilangan qubit dan lihat sama ada kita boleh membuat ramalan klasik tentang nilai pada 30 qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/e5d5f7f5-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/e5d5f7f5-1.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indeed, we see that we have selected a Hamiltonian and state that does not change with the number of qubits. This is a very poor use for a research application of quantum computing, but an excellent one for benchmarking error mitigation techniques. We can confidently use this fixed expectation value as the ideal result, even as we scale up the number of qubits for the testing of error mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Sesungguhnya, kita melihat bahawa kita telah memilih Hamiltonian dan keadaan yang tidak berubah dengan bilangan qubit. Ini penggunaan yang sangat lemah untuk aplikasi penyelidikan pengkomputeran kuantum, tetapi sangat sesuai untuk membuat penanda aras teknik pengurangan ralat. Kita boleh dengan yakin menggunakan nilai jangkaan tetap ini sebagai hasil unggul, walaupun kita menambah bilangan qubit untuk menguji pengurangan ralat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we run this larger circuit with ZNE.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita jalankan litar yang lebih besar ini dengan ZNE.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we run the 30-qubit example with PEC.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, kita jalankan contoh 30 qubit dengan PEC.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d4e98091-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-mitigation/extracted-outputs/d4e98091-0.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Not only did PEC take much longer than the other options, but we clearly reached our maximum overhead threshold. The PEC results paid the overhead price, but the overhead cap prevented sufficiently accurate cancellation of the learned noise model. This is critical. At six qubits, we were able to leverage PEC and get better results with only a modest increase in quantum overhead (about a factor of 5). At 30 qubits, we paid a much higher price (about a factor of 60 times higher) and the results were even worse than the unmitigated estimate. This is not to say that PEC can never work with 30 qubits; that might be circuit-dependent. The message is simply that the exponential growth in quantum overhead makes it difficult to run for large circuits.\n"
msgstr "PEC bukan sahaja mengambil masa yang jauh lebih lama daripada pilihan lain, malah kita jelas mencapai ambang overhed maksimum kita. Keputusan PEC telah membayar harga overhed, tetapi had overhed menghalang pembatalan model hingar yang dipelajari dengan ketepatan yang mencukupi. Ini sangat penting. Pada enam qubit, kita dapat memanfaatkan PEC dan mendapat keputusan yang lebih baik dengan peningkatan overhed kuantum yang sederhana sahaja (kira-kira faktor 5). Pada 30 qubit, kita membayar harga yang jauh lebih tinggi (kira-kira 60 kali lebih tinggi) dan keputusannya malah lebih teruk daripada anggaran tanpa pengurangan. Ini tidak bermakna PEC tidak boleh berfungsi dengan 30 qubit; itu mungkin bergantung pada litar. Mesejnya hanyalah bahawa pertumbuhan eksponen dalam overhed kuantum menyukarkan penjalanan untuk litar besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Key takeaways: {#key-takeaways}"
msgstr "Perkara penting: {#key-takeaways}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurement mitigation often helps and usually carries low overhead: it removes a bias that does not scale with circuit depth and it composes cleanly with nearly everything.\n"
msgstr "Pengurangan pengukuran selalunya membantu dan biasanya mempunyai overhed yang rendah: ia menghapuskan pincang yang tidak berskala dengan kedalaman litar dan ia bergabung dengan baik dengan hampir semua perkara.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some techniques cannot be combined. Even when they can be, make sure you combine them in a consistent way such that one is not undoing the other. A good example is ensuring that twirling is on during the calibration for M3 if those methods are to be combined.\n"
msgstr "Sesetengah teknik tidak boleh digabungkan. Walaupun boleh, pastikan anda menggabungkannya dengan cara yang konsisten supaya satu tidak membatalkan yang lain. Contoh yang baik ialah memastikan twirling dihidupkan semasa penentukuran untuk M3 jika kaedah tersebut hendak digabungkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC and ZNE should be thought of as alternatives to each other. They solve the same problem with opposite tradeoffs:\n"
msgstr "PEC dan ZNE harus dianggap sebagai alternatif antara satu sama lain. Kedua-duanya menyelesaikan masalah yang sama dengan pertukaran yang bertentangan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC: yields unbiased expectation values at the cost of exponential variance.\n"
msgstr "PEC: menghasilkan nilai jangkaan yang tidak berat sebelah dengan kos varians eksponen.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE generally yields residual bias that depends on the extrapolation model, but at moderate cost.\n"
msgstr "ZNE secara amnya menghasilkan pincang baki yang bergantung pada model ekstrapolasi, tetapi dengan kos yang sederhana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "DD can help with long idle periods, but it reshapes the noise model and can invalidate extrapolation or inversion assumptions.\n"
msgstr "DD boleh membantu untuk tempoh melahu yang panjang, tetapi ia membentuk semula model hingar dan boleh membatalkan andaian ekstrapolasi atau penyongsangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling does not reduce noise. It reshapes it and often enables other techniques to work better (ZNE and PEC).\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling tidak mengurangkan hingar. Ia membentuknya semula dan selalunya membolehkan teknik lain berfungsi dengan lebih baik (ZNE dan PEC).\n"
